/* Questions of the Telegram mini app: 50 per training, taken from the
   website's banks. Generated by tools/tg-miniapp/build.py: do not edit. */
window.TG_DATA={"v":1,"n":50,"sets":[{"id":"g_base","sec":"Grammar","title":"Structure & tenses","desc":"Sentence structure, tenses, modals","items":[{"q":"It was not until 1998 ______ the treaty was ratified.","o":["when","that","which","then"],"a":1,"e":"It was not until ... that (emphatic structure)."},{"q":"When you finally get back home, please _____ me a postcard.","o":["to send","send","sent","be sent"],"a":1,"e":"*Imperative*. A request. \"You\" is omitted from the main clause."},{"q":"If you had been here yesterday, you _____ my wife.","o":["could meet","met","will meet","could have met"],"a":3,"e":"\"*If*\" clause. *Past unreal* because of \"yesterday.\""},{"q":"I am scheduled for another ECL next week, _____?","o":["aren't I","amn't I","will I","won't I"],"a":0,"e":"I am, aren't I? This is a strange structure, but that's the way it is."},{"q":"It is my understanding that the subject the students in IDS enjoy the most _____ preposition usage.","o":["are","were","is","am"],"a":2,"e":"\"The subject\" is the simple subject of this sentence."},{"q":"The President can, it is widely believed, in no way, resolve this crisis soon,_____?","o":["can't he","can he","is it","does he"],"a":1,"e":"The phrase \"in no way\" makes the main clause negative, so the tag must be affirmative."},{"q":"Class starts _____ 0730.","o":["in","to","of","at"],"a":3,"e":"When you have an exact time for something, you use \"At.\" The movie ended at :45."},{"q":"I like my coffee _____ milk and sugar.","o":["of","to","for","with"],"a":3,"e":"One thing combined *with* another thing or *with* other things."},{"q":"All of the passengers are _____ board the plane now.","o":["in","at","with","on"],"a":3,"e":"*On board* is a phrase meaning inside a larger vehicle like a plane, train, bus, ship."},{"q":"I think he has a knife _____ his pocket.","o":["in","to","of","for"],"a":0,"e":"*In* a pocket *in* a purse *in* a drawer"},{"q":"Their new business will be located _____ Fulton Street.","o":["at","in","on","for"],"a":2,"e":"Name of the street by itself. No address number given."},{"q":"I want another glass _____ milk.","o":["for","to","with","of"],"a":3,"e":"Something and the item of measurement used for it."},{"q":"He hit me _____ his dictionary, and it was the first time he had ever used it for anything.","o":["with","to","by","at"],"a":0,"e":"The tool or weapon is given. He shot me *with* a rifle."},{"q":"She gave a party _____ her class, all of whom enjoyed themselves.","o":["to","of","for","at"],"a":2,"e":"You can give an activity *for* someone give a party *for* me give a baby shower *for* my sister"},{"q":"He got _____ an argument with his neighbor.","o":["into","of","at","on"],"a":0,"e":"You can *get into* certain things: into trouble into an argument get into debt"},{"q":"Scissors are used _____ cutting paper.","o":["for","at","to","with"],"a":0,"e":"for -ing Something is used to cut Used (in order) to do something"},{"q":"My mother is the lady seated _____ the blue sofa in the corner.","o":["in","on","to","of"],"a":1,"e":"*In* a chair (with arms) *on* a chair (without arms) *on* a sofa (because it's wide and you might not be touching the arms of it)."},{"q":"What should I do _____ a sore throat?","o":["for","of","by","in"],"a":0,"e":"treatment You do something *for* a headache. Or *about* a *cold*."},{"q":"The paratroopers jumped out of the plane _____ hesitation.","o":["for","by","without","under"],"a":2,"e":"We do things either with or without hesitation."},{"q":"What I am asking _____ you is that you be quiet during other people's speeches.","o":["by","of","at","with"],"a":1,"e":"You *ask* something *of* someone. What I'm asking *of* you is that you do your homework."},{"q":"She wore a veil _____ her face.","o":["over","in","at","under"],"a":0,"e":"\"Over\" can mean to *cover* something. He held his hand *over* his mouth."},{"q":"I asked Craig again if the accident _____ his fault.","o":["weren't","wasn't","won't be","hasn't been being"],"a":1,"e":"*Past real* The accident *was* Craig's fault. He just keeps denying it."},{"q":"A dog usually likes to chase cats, and a cat usually likes to chase_____.","o":["trucks","horses","buildings","mice"],"a":3,"e":"Cats would chase mice, not the other 3 objects."},{"q":"Did you _____ a big breakfast this morning?","o":["ate","eats","eaten","eat"],"a":3,"e":"Anytime you use the *do*\" auxiliary, put simple form of the verb. *Do* you *go* to the gym every day? *Did* he *see* that movie?"},{"q":"No matter where you live, you need _____ access to a hospital.","o":["quickly","quick","quickness","quickest"],"a":1,"e":"\"Access\" is a noun. Modify it with an adjective. What kind of access? *Quick* access."},{"q":"Why is the baby crying? Because _____.","o":["he is hungry.","today is Saturday.","the car won't start.","the food was good."],"a":0,"e":"Of these four answers, the only thing to explain a baby's crying would be the *hunger*."},{"q":"Of my four brothers, Danny is _____.","o":["taller","the tallest","the taller","the tall"],"a":1,"e":"four people? Use the superlative. He is *the tallest* one of the four."},{"q":"That shirt, _____ is light blue, costs less than $15.","o":["who","whom","what","which"],"a":3,"e":"\"Which\" is used for things. A shirt is a thing. \"Who\" and \"whom\" are only used for people."},{"q":"I need _____ a car for the weekend.","o":["to rent","rent","renting","rented"],"a":0,"e":"The verb \"need\" requires the infinitive form in this structure."},{"q":"She is very _____.","o":["study","studious","student","studying"],"a":1,"e":"You need an adjective here. \"Studious\" is the adjective form of \"study."},{"q":"I had the secretary _____ the letter five times.","o":["retyping","retypes","retyped","retype"],"a":3,"e":"You have somebody *do* something (simple form). I had the barber *cut* my hair *cancel* my credit card."},{"q":"If you want to mail that letter, you will have to use three _____.","o":["twenty-cents stamps","twenties-cent stamp","twenty-cent stamps","twenty-cent stamp"],"a":2,"e":"When you turn a number into part of a hyphenated adjective, you drop the plural of the *mile* run"},{"q":"Mrs. Barrow is a great painter, and _____.","o":["so her daughter is","so is her daughter","so does her daughter","her daughter do too"],"a":1,"e":"The main clause contains the \"*Be*\" verb, so the second abridged clause must also"},{"q":"I think these questions are the _____ of all the questions I have tried.","o":["more difficult","most difficult","difficultest","difficulter"],"a":1,"e":"*Superlative* : The adjective is 3 syllables long, so you must use \"*Most*\" to express car I have ever seen. She is *the most intelligent* person I have ever met."},{"q":"The cause of all the recent accidents at several major airports_____ not been determined yet.","o":["is","has","have","were"],"a":1,"e":"*Cause* is the simple subject. The verb must agree with *cause*. The *cause has* not been determined."},{"q":"_____ the test, he stood up and left the room.","o":["Finish","Finished","Having finished","Being finish"],"a":2,"e":"This started out as the clause *after he had finished the test* We can reduced it to the phrase *having finished*"},{"q":"The drill instructor is very angry. He is _____.","o":["upset","happy","handsome","intelligent"],"a":0,"e":"angry = upset = mad = furious = very unhappy"},{"q":"Is the material *flammable*? _____ No, it is _____.","o":["inflammable","deflammable","nonflammable","unflammable"],"a":2,"e":"flammable = it *will* burn *no*Nflammable = it will *not* burn Do not be flames. *Flammable* and *inflammable* mean the *same thing*!"},{"q":"Video cameras are used in many stores to _____ shoplifting.","o":["deter","detour","defer","demure"],"a":0,"e":"*Deter* = to try to prevent something from happening"},{"q":"I have _____ about question #2.","o":["a doubt","a root","a dude","a crunch"],"a":0,"e":"*A doubt* = an uncertainty = not knowing something"},{"q":"That painting is counterfeit! It's an obvious _____!","o":["treasure","masterpiece","delight","fake"],"a":3,"e":"*Counterfeit* = fake = not genuine = bogus = phony = not real"},{"q":"The Titanic is lying two-and-a-half miles _____ the surface of the water.","o":["above","in","with","beneath"],"a":3,"e":"*Beneath* = *under* = *below* = *underneath*"},{"q":"He comes to class every morning _____ foot.","o":["on","in","at","with"],"a":0,"e":"means of transportation *on* foot *but by car by bicycle*"},{"q":"Is this CD player very expensive? _____ No, it is _____.","o":["cheap","nice","costly","priceless"],"a":0,"e":"Opposite of expensive = cheap costly = expensive"},{"q":"What is the *subject* of her speech?","o":["length","purpose","topic","source"],"a":2,"e":"subject = topic = what you are talking about"},{"q":"The traffic was extremely heavy. There were _____ cars on the road.","o":["too much","few","too few","too many"],"a":3,"e":"*Cars* = count noun Heavy traffic means *too many cars*."},{"q":"If the water is vaporized, we can call it _____.","o":["ice","frozen","steam","cold"],"a":2,"e":"vapor = steam Choices A, B, and D all involve *cold*. Only C involves *heat*."},{"q":"I am scheduled to take one more OPI, _____?","o":["am not I","aren't I","am I","are I"],"a":1,"e":"exception I AM, *aren't I*? More formal = I AM< *AM I not*?"},{"q":"My glass is empty. Please _____ again. I'm thirsty.","o":["wait on it","run it out","fill it up","chip it in"],"a":2,"e":"*Fill* up = replenish = put something in an empty space"},{"q":"Can we go _____ you to the movies?","o":["apart from","along with","due to","apart at"],"a":1,"e":"go along with = phrasal verb meaning to accompany"}]},{"id":"g_plus","sec":"Grammar","title":"Grammar Plus","desc":"Conditionals, passive, reported speech","items":[{"q":"If I _______ you, I would accept that assignment.","o":["were","was","am","be"],"a":0,"e":"Second conditional: 'If I were you' (subjunctive 'were' for all persons)."},{"q":"The suspect _______ by the military police right now.","o":["is being questioned","is questioning","questions","has questioned"],"a":0,"e":"Passive, present continuous: is being + past participle."},{"q":"The more you train, the _______ you become.","o":["stronger","strongest","more strong","most strong"],"a":0,"e":"Parallel comparative: 'The more..., the stronger...'."},{"q":"This is the third time this month that the generator ______ during a storm.","o":["has failed","fails","had failed","will fail"],"a":0,"e":"'This is the first / second / third time (that)...' is followed by the present perfect."},{"q":"I barely recognized Major Tran at the reunion; he ______ a lot of weight since our academy days.","o":["had lost","was losing","loses","would lose"],"a":0,"e":"A change completed before a past moment (the reunion), counted 'since' an earlier time: past perfect."},{"q":"When you get home, the kids ______, so please try not to slam the door.","o":["will probably be sleeping","will probably have slept","had probably slept","probably sleep"],"a":0,"e":"An action in progress at a future moment (when you get home): future continuous."},{"q":"She assured us that by Friday she ______ all the paperwork, but on Friday nothing was ready.","o":["would have completed","will have completed","has completed","had been completing"],"a":0,"e":"Future perfect in the past: would have + past participle (completion by a time that is now past)."},{"q":"Ever since the new road ______, traffic past the main gate has more than doubled.","o":["opened","has opened","had opened","was opening"],"a":0,"e":"'Since' + a point in the past takes the simple past; the main clause takes the present perfect."},{"q":"I ______ drink so much coffee before I started working night shifts.","o":["didn't use to","wasn't used to","don't use to","didn't get used to"],"a":0,"e":"Negative of 'used to': didn't use to + base verb (no -d after did)."},{"q":"If I spoke Arabic, I ______ for the liaison job in Qatar last year.","o":["would have been chosen","would be chosen","will have been chosen","had been chosen"],"a":0,"e":"Present unreal fact (I don't speak Arabic) + past result: would have been + past participle (passive)."},{"q":"So heavy ______ that the flight to Anchorage was canceled.","o":["was the snowfall","the snowfall was","did the snowfall","had the snowfall"],"a":0,"e":"So + adjective at the start of the sentence: invert be and the subject (So heavy was the snowfall that ...)."},{"q":"______ the mechanic checked the brakes before the trip, the truck wouldn't be in the ditch now.","o":["Had","Has","Should","Were"],"a":0,"e":"Had + subject + past participle = If the mechanic had checked (past condition), with a present result (now)."},{"q":"That ______ Sergeant Kim at the door; she said she'd stop by around six.","o":["must be","must have","can be","should have been"],"a":0,"e":"must be: a confident present deduction; 'can' is not used for a specific deduction."},{"q":"______ from his accent, the new instructor grew up somewhere near Boston.","o":["Judging","Judged","Having judged","Judge"],"a":0,"e":"Judging from/by is a fixed participle phrase meaning 'based on what we can see or hear'."},{"q":"What happened ______ that the truck ran out of fuel ten miles from camp.","o":["was","is being","had","did"],"a":0,"e":"What happened was (that) ...: a what-cleft that presents an event."},{"q":"Most of the cadets travel home ______ train during the holidays.","o":["by","on","in","with"],"a":0,"e":"Means of transportation without an article takes 'by': by train ('on the train' needs the article)."},{"q":"How ______ luggage are you allowed to bring on the flight?","o":["much","many","few","more"],"a":0,"e":"'Luggage' is uncountable, so ask 'how much'."},{"q":"If the clinic ______ better, patients wouldn't have to wait three weeks for an appointment.","o":["were staffed","is staffed","had staffed","would be staffed"],"a":0,"e":"Second conditional in the passive: if + were + past participle."},{"q":"We ______ lost right now if you had brought the map as I asked you to.","o":["wouldn't be","wouldn't have been","won't be","aren't"],"a":0,"e":"Mixed conditional: past condition (had brought), present result (wouldn't be ... right now)."},{"q":"______ GPS, most of us would be completely lost in an unfamiliar city.","o":["Without","Unless","Except","Instead of"],"a":0,"e":"Without + noun can replace an if-clause: Without GPS = If we didn't have GPS."},{"q":"Unless the lab results ______ any problems, you can return to full duty on Monday.","o":["show","don't show","won't show","didn't show"],"a":0,"e":"Unless already means 'if not', so the verb stays affirmative; present simple for the future."},{"q":"The pilots carry survival kits *in case* they have to eject over the ocean.","o":["because they might","on the condition that they","even though they","only after they"],"a":0,"e":"In case = as a precaution because something might happen."},{"q":"By the end of next year, every radio in the battalion ______ with a digital model.","o":["will have been replaced","will have replaced","will be replacing","has been replaced"],"a":0,"e":"Future perfect passive (will have been + past participle) for an action completed before a future time."},{"q":"During basic training, recruits ______ the obstacle course again whenever anyone in the squad fell behind.","o":["were made to run","were made run","made to run","were made running"],"a":0,"e":"Make someone do -> passive 'be made TO do': the 'to' comes back in the passive."},{"q":"______ your teeth cleaned twice a year is fully covered by the military dental plan.","o":["Having","Have","Had","To having"],"a":0,"e":"Gerund subject with a causative: Having + object + past participle + singular verb (is)."},{"q":"All the glass from the broken window is outside the house, so the burglar ______ that way.","o":["can't have broken in","must have broken in","can't have broke in","shouldn't have broken in"],"a":0,"e":"Can't have + past participle (broken, not broke): a logical conclusion that something did not happen."},{"q":"Your Spanish is excellent! You ______ in Latin America for years.","o":["must have lived","can't have lived","must live","should have lived"],"a":0,"e":"Must have + past participle: a confident deduction from evidence (your excellent Spanish)."},{"q":"You ______ during the safety briefing instead of texting your girlfriend!","o":["should have been listening","must have been listening","should had been listening","should have listen"],"a":0,"e":"Should have been + -ing: criticism of what someone was (not) doing at a past time."},{"q":"When I met him in 2015, Tom told me he ______ speak three languages, but he has forgotten most of his French since then.","o":["could","can","was able","has been able to"],"a":0,"e":"'Can' becomes 'could' after a past reporting verb, especially when the fact is no longer true."},{"q":"The customs officer wanted to know how long ______ in the country.","o":["I planned to stay","did I plan to stay","I did plan staying","was I planning to stay"],"a":0,"e":"In a reported question there is no 'did' and no inversion: how long I planned to stay."},{"q":"I wonder ______ so quiet today; he usually never stops talking.","o":["why the sergeant is","why is the sergeant","why the sergeant does","why does the sergeant"],"a":0,"e":"After 'I wonder', use statement order: why the sergeant is so quiet."},{"q":"Let's take a ten-minute break before the next block of instruction, ______?","o":["shall we","will we","don't we","do we"],"a":0,"e":"A suggestion with 'Let's' takes the tag 'shall we?'."},{"q":"She'd never miss a formation without calling first, ______?","o":["would she","had she","wouldn't she","did she"],"a":0,"e":"'She'd' + base verb = she would; with 'never' the tag is positive: would she?"},{"q":"______ was at the meeting besides the commander?","o":["Who else","Else who","Whom else","Who other"],"a":0,"e":"'Else' follows the question word; 'who' (not 'whom') is the subject of 'was'."},{"q":"The lieutenant tried her best ______ calm when the radio reported enemy contact.","o":["to stay","staying","stay","stayed"],"a":0,"e":"try (one's best) + to-infinitive = make an effort to do something difficult."},{"q":"After three hours of digging, the squad finally managed ______ the truck out of the mud.","o":["to get","getting","get","to getting"],"a":0,"e":"manage + to-infinitive = succeed in doing something difficult."},{"q":"Specialist Lee went to the education center ______ about tuition assistance for night classes.","o":["to ask","for asking","for ask","to asking"],"a":0,"e":"Use the to-infinitive to express a person's purpose, not 'for + -ing'."},{"q":"The officer to ______ you should address your leave request is Captain Ruiz.","o":["whom","who","that","which"],"a":0,"e":"After a preposition, use whom for people (which for things); never 'that'."},{"q":"Dr. Patel, ______ many of you met at the clinic, will lead tomorrow's first-aid class.","o":["whom","whose","which","that"],"a":0,"e":"whom is the object of 'met'; that cannot be used in a non-defining clause."},{"q":"We're having a barbecue with ______ Johnsons, our new neighbors from across the street, on Saturday.","o":["the","a","an","(no article)"],"a":0,"e":"A family name in the plural takes 'the': the Johnsons = the Johnson family."},{"q":"The new barracks are modern, but ______ soldiers want to live there because they're so far from the gym and the dining facility.","o":["few","a few","little","a little"],"a":0,"e":"'Few' (without 'a') is negative: almost no soldiers. 'Little' is used with uncountable nouns."},{"q":"Every officer and every NCO in the battalion ______ expected to attend the change-of-command ceremony.","o":["is","are","were","have been"],"a":0,"e":"Subjects with 'every' (even 'every X and every Y') take a singular verb."},{"q":"______ the end of the movie, almost everyone in the theater was in tears.","o":["At","In","On","To"],"a":0,"e":"'At the end of + noun' = at the final point of something. 'In the end' (without 'of') means 'finally'."},{"q":"Several soldiers objected ______ moved to the older barracks on the far side of post.","o":["to being","to be","for being","from being"],"a":0,"e":"'Object to' is followed by a gerund because 'to' is a preposition here: object to being moved."},{"q":"There is a growing demand ______ soldiers who can speak Korean or Japanese.","o":["for","of","to","on"],"a":0,"e":"The noun 'demand' takes 'for': a demand for linguists."},{"q":"The pilot could not see the runway ______ the thick fog, so she diverted to another airfield.","o":["because of","although","despite","whereas"],"a":0,"e":"Because of + noun gives the reason; despite would show contrast, which makes no sense here, and although / whereas need a clause."},{"q":"Captain Reyes is ______ officer in the battalion, but she already commands a company.","o":["the youngest","the younger","the most young","younger"],"a":0,"e":"One-syllable adjectives form the superlative with -est: young - the youngest."},{"q":"We will need ______ more volunteers if we want to finish loading the trucks before dark.","o":["many","much","very","so"],"a":0,"e":"Many more + plural countable noun (volunteers); much more is for uncountable nouns."},{"q":"Only by working through the night ______ to meet the deadline for the inspection.","o":["were we able","we were able","we could","able we were"],"a":0,"e":"Only by + -ing at the start causes inversion: were we able."},{"q":"______ was the demand for the new tablets that the PX sold out within an hour.","o":["Such","So","So much","How"],"a":0,"e":"Such + be + noun ... that (inversion) means 'the demand was so great that ...'."}]},{"id":"g_topics","sec":"Grammar","title":"Grammar by topic","desc":"Prepositions, tenses, modals and more","items":[{"q":"The convoy ______ the checkpoint when the ambush started.","o":["approaches","was approaching","has approached","approach"],"a":1,"e":"An action in progress that is interrupted takes the past progressive.","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"This time next week we ______ across the Mediterranean.","o":["sail","will sail","will be sailing","have sailed"],"a":2,"e":"An action in progress at a future moment.","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"When I ______ home tonight, I will call you.","o":["will get","get","am getting","got"],"a":1,"e":"After when with future meaning, use the present simple.","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"Once the order ______, we will execute it immediately.","o":["will arrive","arrives","arrived","is arriving"],"a":1,"e":"Once + present carries a future meaning.","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"In our ethics class, we were taught that a good leader should have _____.","o":["breadth","timber","integrity","ground"],"a":2,"e":"*Integrity* = honesty = sincerity = inner truth = basic morality","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"Cpl. Whitfield _____ next week.","o":["graduate","graduated","will graduate","is graduate"],"a":2,"e":"\"Next week\" requires *future tense*. *He will graduate*","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"I have been here at DLI _____ 8 weeks.","o":["since","for","with","during"],"a":1,"e":"When you have the total amount of time given, use *for* in these *present perfect* structures.","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"The teacher _____ all day yesterday preparing new handouts for you.","o":["work","worked","works","working"],"a":1,"e":"yesterday = past tense third person singular *the teacher worked*","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"I have been here _____ two months.","o":["since","during","for","at"],"a":2,"e":"starting point, you use \"*Since*.\" I have been here *since* April 5.","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"By the time you graduate, you _____ at least 40 tests.","o":["took","will be taking","will have taken","would have taken"],"a":2,"e":"future perfect tense By the time I retire, I will have worked for this company for 35 years.","t":"Tenses"},{"q":"You ______ salute a senior officer; it is a regulation.","o":["might","must","could","may"],"a":1,"e":"An absolute obligation, such as a regulation: must.","t":"Modals"},{"q":"You ______ better check the coordinates twice.","o":["would","had","should","must"],"a":1,"e":"had better + the simple form of the verb (had better check).","t":"Modals"},{"q":"If you are tired, you _____.","o":["would rest","must to rest","should rest","would have rest"],"a":2,"e":"Advice. \"Should\" is a common modal when giving advice. If these questions are too easy, you *should go* to a higher level.","t":"Modals"},{"q":"What will you _____ tomorrow night?","o":["doing","do","done","to do"],"a":1,"e":"modal Put simple form after a modal. You will *do* what?","t":"Modals"},{"q":"They _____ the whole report already! It was only assigned this morning.","o":["can't have read","mustn't read","mustn't be reading","should have read"],"a":0,"e":"*Can't have* + past participle expresses certainty that something did not happen.","t":"Modals"},{"q":"This bridge ______ in 1952.","o":["is built","was built","has built","built"],"a":1,"e":"A date in the past: past passive, was built.","t":"Passive"},{"q":"We liked the restaurant because we _____ quickly.","o":["are serve","have being served","were served","had been being serve"],"a":2,"e":"Past tense passive voice They served us quickly (active) = We were served quickly (passive).","t":"Passive"},{"q":"This question _____ for you by Mr. Ashford.","o":["is wrote","was written","was wrote","writes"],"a":1,"e":"*Passive voice* . Something *is done* by somebody. *Past tense* of the *passive*. It *was done* by somebody.","t":"Passive"},{"q":"The runway _____ when the delegation landed.","o":["is repaired","was being repaired","has been repaired","repairs"],"a":1,"e":"An action in progress in the past, interrupted by another, takes the past continuous, here in the passive.","t":"Passive"},{"q":"If that thief hadn't tricked me, I ______ in prison now.","o":["wouldn't be","wouldn't have been","won't be","am not"],"a":0,"e":"Mixed conditional: past condition, present result.","t":"Conditionals"},{"q":"If only I ______ listened to your advice!","o":["have","had","would","did"],"a":1,"e":"If only + past perfect expresses regret about the past.","t":"Conditionals"},{"q":"They will not qualify him because his ECL is still _____ 80.","o":["to","behind","with","under"],"a":3,"e":"A number can be *under* (below) another number: his ECL score is under 80. The temperature is below zero.","t":"Conditionals"},{"q":"_____, I would have helped you.","o":["Had I been there","If I was there","If I were there","Was I there"],"a":0,"e":"This is the *reduced subjuntive*. \"If I had been there\" can be reduced to \"Had I been there.","t":"Conditionals"},{"q":"\"Do you like tea?\" -> He asked her ______ she liked tea.","o":["that","if","what","which"],"a":1,"e":"A yes/no question is reported with if or whether.","t":"Reported speech"},{"q":"\"Water boils at 100 C,\" he said. -> He said water ______ at 100 C.","o":["boiled","boils","had boiled","would boil"],"a":1,"e":"A general truth does not change tense in reported speech.","t":"Reported speech"},{"q":"Last week, he promised me that he _____ attend yesterday's meeting.","o":["will","was going","did","would"],"a":3,"e":"Reported speech: the reporting verb *promised* is in the past, so *will* becomes *would*.","t":"Reported speech"},{"q":"He has been in the Navy ______ 2008.","o":["for","since","from","during"],"a":1,"e":"since + a starting point in time (since 2008); for + a length of time (for six years).","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"The score was *tied* at the end of regulation time.","o":["lopsided","undetermined","even","inconsequential"],"a":2,"e":"*Tied* = to be even, to be the same. The score was *tied* at 2-2. His home run in the eleventh inning finally broke the 3-3 tie.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"A major *is lower in rank than* a colonel.","o":["is over","is ahead of","is under","is up to"],"a":2,"e":"*To be under* = to be the subordinate = to be lower = to be underneath in the chain- of-command","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"By the time the firemen arrived, the flames _____ by the homeowner.","o":["had been extinguished","are extinguishing","were extinguish","will be extinguishing"],"a":0,"e":"Two actions in the past. The first action (in time) can be *past perfect*. The subsequent action can be simple past.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"My parents live _____ 253 Oak Street.","o":["on","in","at","to"],"a":2,"e":"If you have the *number* and the street name, it takes *at*.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"My father always takes a long nap _____ the afternoon.","o":["in","at","of","with"],"a":0,"e":"part of the day *in* the morning *in* the afternoon *in* the evening","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"We might be able to travel quickly to the moon _____ the future.","o":["of","in","to","on"],"a":1,"e":"a period of time *in* the past In the future","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"Sign your name _____ block 21 at the bottom of this page.","o":["on","in","for","to"],"a":1,"e":"The block has a perimeter, so you put your signature *in* the block.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"The contractors are going to tear _____ the old road and replace it with a modern 4-lane one.","o":["down","up","over","off"],"a":1,"e":"The road is lying flat *on* the ground, so you have to tear it *up*.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"Craig looks *down in the dumps* today.","o":["rich","unhappy","talented","angry"],"a":1,"e":"*Down in the dumps* = unhappy = sad = dejected = in a depressing situation, as if one is *living in the dump*.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"My favorite season of the year is *autumn*.","o":["winter","spring","summer","fall"],"a":3,"e":"seasons of the year *fall* = *autumn* (September, October, November in the U.S.)","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"Blake is 17 years old. Neil is 18 years old. Craig is 16 years old.","o":["Neil is younger than Blake.","Blake is older than Neil.","Craig is younger than Neil.","Craig is older than Blake."],"a":2,"e":"Craig (16) is younger than Neil (18). Neil is the oldest and Craig is the youngest.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"It is not polite to stare _____ strangers.","o":["for","with","at","on"],"a":2,"e":"*Stare at*, *look at*, *point at*: these verbs take *at* before the person or thing.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"I visited my family _____ Christmas.","o":["in","to","of","for"],"a":3,"e":"preposition of time *for* a short period of *time*.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"Nadia has worked at the hospital ever _____ she graduated.","o":["from","when","since","ago"],"a":2,"e":"*Ever since* links a present situation to its starting point in the past.","t":"Prepositions"},{"q":"We have ______ time before the briefing.","o":["a few","few","little","many"],"a":2,"e":"time is uncountable with a negative sense, so little.","t":"Determiners"},{"q":"______ information you gave me was very useful.","o":["A","An","The","-"],"a":2,"e":"Something already known (a definite reference) takes the.","t":"Determiners"},{"q":"This frigate is ______ than the previous one.","o":["more fast","faster","fastest","the fastest"],"a":1,"e":"Short adjective, so the comparative takes -er.","t":"Structure"},{"q":"Let's not _____ the decision until we have the full report.","o":["taking","to take","taken","take"],"a":3,"e":"The negative form is *let's not* + base form.","t":"Structure"},{"q":"This is _____ route to the airport at this hour.","o":["fast","faster","the fastest","the most fast"],"a":2,"e":"Short adjectives form the superlative with *-est*: the fastest.","t":"Structure"},{"q":"_____ he had trained for months, he failed the swimming test.","o":["Despite","Even though","In spite","Therefore"],"a":1,"e":"Only *even though* can introduce a subject and a conjugated verb.","t":"Structure"},{"q":"The committee demanded that the report _____ immediately.","o":["is published","publishes","be published","has been published"],"a":2,"e":"The subjunctive passive is *be* + past participle: that it be published.","t":"Structure"},{"q":"I do not remember _____ that decision. When was it made?","o":["to make","making","I had made","we are making"],"a":1,"e":"*Remember* + -ing refers to a memory of something already done. With the infinitive it would mean not forgetting to do it.","t":"Structure"},{"q":"My sister ______ in Milan for two months last year.","o":["is","was","had","did"],"a":1,"e":"last year + a state (be): simple past, was.","t":"Simple past"}]},{"id":"v_ctx","sec":"Vocabulary","title":"Vocabulary in context","desc":"Words and their meaning in a sentence","items":[{"q":"We found a *flaw* in the structural design.","o":["insect","error","tool","change"],"a":1,"e":"*A flaw* is a mistake, error, something wrong."},{"q":"You must keep the *aisle* clear.","o":["surface","walkway","sofa","fence"],"a":1,"e":"An *aisle* is a long narrow space between chairs, usually in a theater, in a church, in an auditorium"},{"q":"The floor is covered with *splinters*.","o":["water","dead flowers","spilled food","small pieces of wood"],"a":3,"e":"*Spinters* are very small pieces of wood, created when you are whittling, sawing, chopping"},{"q":"Here's some news. It's hot off the press.","o":["It's incorrect.","It's the most recent.","It's unbelievable.","It's funny."],"a":1,"e":"News that is hot off the press has just been printed and often contains the most recent information about something."},{"q":"The boss sent me off on some wild goose chase.","o":["I was given a great assignment.","I was given an impossible task.","I was given a promotion and a raise.","I was given extra help with my job."],"a":1,"e":"wild-goose chase / a search which is completely unsuccessful and a waste of time because the person or thing being searched for does not exist or is somewhere else"},{"q":"How old is your father?","o":["He has 67 years.","He is being 67 years.","He is 67.","He does 67."],"a":2,"e":"In English, we do our ages with the *be* verb, not the *have* verb. My car *is* four years when she died."},{"q":"Her testimony corroborated the earlier statement.","o":["confirmed","contradicted","replaced","questioned"],"a":0,"e":"Corroborate = confirm with further evidence."},{"q":"The negotiations reached a deadlock.","o":["a standstill","an agreement","a conclusion","a compromise"],"a":0,"e":"Deadlock = a situation in which no progress is possible."},{"q":"The regulation supersedes all previous versions.","o":["replaces","confirms","completes","cancels partly"],"a":0,"e":"Supersede = replace an older rule or version."},{"q":"Their cooperation has been invaluable.","o":["extremely useful","worthless","occasional","expected"],"a":0,"e":"Invaluable = extremely useful. Careful, it does not mean without value."},{"q":"Because of the heavy rain, we will have to *cancel* the parade.","o":["call off","put off","delay","postpone"],"a":0,"e":"cancel = call off ((postpone = put off))"},{"q":"The milk tastes *sour*.","o":["unpleasant","delicious","sweet","good"],"a":0,"e":"sour = bad = not good = gone bad (for milk) *sour* (for lemon or lime) means *tart*, *tangy*, \"attacks\" the tongue"},{"q":"*I rarely* go to movies during the weekend.","o":["seldom","usually","from time to time","often"],"a":0,"e":"*Rarely* = *seldom*, not very often, only once in a blue moon"},{"q":"I _____ a new car last week.","o":["buy","bought","buyed","was buy"],"a":1,"e":"Time words \"last week\" require *past tense*."},{"q":"If the food is rotten, what should you probably do to it?","o":["Eat it.","Serve it.","Save it.","Throw it out."],"a":3,"e":"rotten = spoiled = not good = probably cannot be eaten"},{"q":"Children should not play near the dump with *bare* feet.","o":["naked","unwashed","healthy","two"],"a":0,"e":"bare = naked = not covered with clothing = exposed"},{"q":"There was a *blizzard* last night.","o":["light shower","heavy snowstorm","raging flood","mild breeze"],"a":1,"e":"blizzard = a lot of snow driven by strong winds"},{"q":"We *spotted* the enemy sniper at a sixteenth-floor window.","o":["detected","drew","shot","sent"],"a":0,"e":"*To spot* = to see, to detect, to discern at a distance"},{"q":"The police found a corpse behind the Bellamy Theater.","o":["killer","dead person","military person","vehicle"],"a":1,"e":"*Corpse* = dead person, body (dead body)"},{"q":"He gave a *dazzling* speech.","o":["brilliant","hideous","very bad","prolonged"],"a":0,"e":"dazzling = brilliant = impressive = extremely good = great"},{"q":"We need to *boost* morale around here.","o":["measure","lower","raise","evaluate"],"a":2,"e":"boost = raise = increase A booster rocket a booster shot I can't reach the highest shelf. Give me a *boost*."},{"q":"I got *drenched* last night as I was walking home from the movies.","o":["soaked","lost","dizzy","lonely"],"a":0,"e":"*Drenched* means very wet; to make someone or something extremely wet"},{"q":"He was very sick; *therefore*, he couldn't compete in the race.","o":["yet","however","since","thus"],"a":3,"e":"*Therefore* = *thus*, so, as a result, because of this, consequently"},{"q":"Some of these questions are *bewildering*.","o":["easy","amusing","long","confusing"],"a":3,"e":"bewildering = confusing = not easy to understand"},{"q":"There was a typical *snafu* about the out processing schedules.","o":["success","good arrangement","problem","routine"],"a":2,"e":"snafu = typical problem = acronym for \"Situation Normal : All Fouled Up.\" *S-n-a-f- u*."},{"q":"Don't drag your feet.","o":["Don't hurry.","Don't run.","Don't stumble.","Don't delay."],"a":3,"e":"to drag your feet = to delay = to do something slowly"},{"q":"He is not telling the truth.","o":["He is jogging.","He is starving.","He is lying.","He is working."],"a":2,"e":"to lie = to *not* tell the truth = to say untrue things"},{"q":"That is a *confusing* math problem.","o":["easy","perplexing","boring","simple"],"a":1,"e":"confusing = perplexing = hard to understand = difficult to decipher"},{"q":"She brought up an important point during the meeting. “Bring up” means:","o":["mention / raise","criticize","reject","write down"],"a":0,"e":"Bring up = mention a topic (also: raise a child)."},{"q":"He made up an excuse for being late. “Make up” here means:","o":["invent","accept","repeat","apologize"],"a":0,"e":"Make up = invent (a story, an excuse); also: reconcile."},{"q":"Fighting broke out near the border at dawn. “Break out” means:","o":["start suddenly","stop completely","move south","calm down"],"a":0,"e":"Break out = begin suddenly (war, fire, epidemic)."},{"q":"He really takes after his father. “Take after” means:","o":["resemble (a parent)","obey","follow physically","admire"],"a":0,"e":"Take after = look or behave like an older family member."},{"q":"Please draw up a new plan. “Draw up” means:","o":["prepare in writing","cancel","shorten","approve"],"a":0,"e":"Draw up = prepare in writing (a plan, a report, a contract)."},{"q":"Report to the supervisor *promptly*.","o":["right away","when you feel like it","eventually","as late as you like"],"a":0,"e":"promptly = right away = quickly = as soon as possible = without delay"},{"q":"That new sonar system cost an arm and a leg. It was:","o":["extremely expensive","slightly damaged","bought on credit","a bargain"],"a":0,"e":"Cost an arm and a leg = be very expensive."},{"q":"The protest got out of hand very quickly. It:","o":["became impossible to control","ended peacefully","was well organized","was postponed"],"a":0,"e":"Get out of hand = become uncontrollable."},{"q":"We passed the inspection by the skin of our teeth. That is:","o":["only just / barely","with an excellent score","thanks to the dentist","without any effort"],"a":0,"e":"By the skin of your teeth = by a very narrow margin."},{"q":"The transfer order came out of the blue. It was:","o":["completely unexpected","sent by the navy","delayed","predictable"],"a":0,"e":"Out of the blue = suddenly, without warning."},{"q":"Skip the details and cut to the chase. “Cut to the chase” means:","o":["get to the main point","end the meeting","start running","lower your voice"],"a":0,"e":"Cut to the chase = go directly to the essential point."},{"q":"Give me a ballpark figure for the repair costs. This means:","o":["a rough estimate","an exact amount","the maximum price","a written invoice"],"a":0,"e":"Ballpark figure = approximate number (from baseball)."},{"q":"It took the new ensign a month to learn the ropes. This means:","o":["learn how the job is done","study knots only","get physically fit","memorize the ranks"],"a":0,"e":"Learn the ropes = learn the basics of a job (nautical origin)."},{"q":"The president hesitated to put boots on the ground. This means:","o":["deploy ground troops","buy new equipment","inspect the barracks","order new uniforms"],"a":0,"e":"Boots on the ground = soldiers physically deployed in an area."},{"q":"He was left holding the bag. This means:","o":["he took the blame alone","he received a reward","he was promoted","he resigned"],"a":0,"e":"Be left holding the bag = be left to take the blame alone."},{"q":"The talks hit a snag. This means:","o":["met an unexpected problem","ended successfully","were cancelled","were rushed"],"a":0,"e":"Hit a snag = meet an unexpected problem."},{"q":"Excessive noise is _____ to concentration.","o":["responsible","harmful","incredible","efficient"],"a":1,"e":"*Harmful to* means damaging to something."},{"q":"Please _____ that all the windows are closed before you leave.","o":["affect","undergo","ensure","maintain"],"a":2,"e":"*Ensure that* means make certain that. *Undergo* means to experience."},{"q":"The witness could not give an _____ account of the incident.","o":["capable","accurate","conscious","prior"],"a":1,"e":"*Accurate* means exact and free from error. *Prior* means earlier."},{"q":"The course is designed to help officers _____ their leadership skills.","o":["grow","spread","develop","stretch"],"a":2,"e":"Skills are *developed*. *Grow* and *stretch* are not used with abilities acquired through training."},{"q":"On whose _____ was the door opened?","o":["majority","superiority","authority","inferiority"],"a":2,"e":"*On whose authority* asks who gave the order or the right to act."},{"q":"Fatigue is one of the lasting _____ of the illness.","o":["delay effects","over effects","after effects","down effects"],"a":2,"e":"*After-effects* are the effects that remain once the cause has passed."}]},{"id":"v_mil","sec":"Vocabulary","title":"American & military","desc":"Words of everyday and military life","items":[{"q":"The platoon conducted a reconnaissance mission near the border. “Reconnaissance” means:","o":["exploration to gather information","a direct assault","a supply delivery","a training drill"],"a":0,"e":"Reconnaissance = observing an area to collect intelligence (recon)."},{"q":"He is on leave this week. “Leave” means:","o":["authorized absence from duty","a disciplinary sanction","night duty","a training course"],"a":0,"e":"Leave = official permission to be absent (vacation)."},{"q":"Follow the chain of command. The “chain of command” is:","o":["the official line of authority","a security fence","a radio network","a supply route"],"a":0,"e":"Chain of command = hierarchy through which orders pass."},{"q":"A “beachhead” is:","o":["a position secured on a hostile shore","a naval base","a coastal radar","a landing craft"],"a":0,"e":"Beachhead = a position secured on an enemy shore."},{"q":"A “quartermaster” is responsible for:","o":["supplies and provisions","navigation only","artillery","intelligence"],"a":0,"e":"Quartermaster = the person responsible for supplies and provisions."},{"q":"The day after his promotion to sergeant, he sewed the new *chevrons* onto his dress uniform.","o":["V-shaped stripes showing enlisted rank","small metal badges awarded for good shooting","colored ribbons for campaigns served","cloth tapes printed with his last name"],"a":0,"e":"Chevrons are the V-shaped stripes that mark the rank of corporals and sergeants."},{"q":"The *sentry* at the fuel point stopped the truck and asked the driver for the password.","o":["a soldier on guard duty","a traffic controller","a supply clerk","a civilian receptionist"],"a":0,"e":"A sentry is a soldier posted to keep watch and control who passes; a common synonym is 'guard'."},{"q":"If your GPS stops working, use your map and ______ to find north and stay on course.","o":["compass","calendar","clipboard","calculator"],"a":0,"e":"A compass is an instrument with a needle that points to magnetic north."},{"q":"Report to the *motor pool* at 0600 to sign out your vehicle for the convoy.","o":["where unit vehicles are parked and maintained","a list of drivers who are available for duty","the fuel station near the main gate","the office that issues driver's licenses"],"a":0,"e":"A motor pool is the area where a unit keeps, services and dispatches its vehicles."},{"q":"He set up an *allotment* so that part of his monthly pay goes straight to his wife's bank account.","o":["a part of pay sent automatically","a small garden rented from the town","a pay increase for married soldiers","a loan approved by the base bank"],"a":0,"e":"A pay allotment is a fixed amount of a service member's pay sent automatically to a person or account every month."},{"q":"Make sure your gear is *squared away* before the colonel walks through the barracks.","o":["neat and in good order","packed and ready to ship","returned to the supply room","labeled with your name"],"a":0,"e":"Squared away (American military slang) = neat, organized and ready; said of a person, it means competent and well prepared."},{"q":"The hospital and the gym are the two busiest buildings on the *installation*.","o":["the military base","the new equipment being put in","the main parking area","the family housing area"],"a":0,"e":"In U.S. military English, an installation is a base or post. In everyday English it also means the act of installing something."},{"q":"During the ______ exercise, Marines came ashore from the ships in landing craft.","o":["amphibious","ambiguous","ambitious","anonymous"],"a":0,"e":"Amphibious operations move forces from the sea onto land."},{"q":"The bugle call known as ______ wakes the soldiers at 0530 and starts the duty day.","o":["reveille","revenue","revelation","revival"],"a":0,"e":"Reveille (REV-uh-lee in American English) is the morning bugle call that signals the start of the day."},{"q":"Our dog dug three holes in the back ______ while we were at work, and now the lawn looks terrible.","o":["yard","porch","hallway","driveway"],"a":0,"e":"Yard (US) = the grassy area around a house (UK: garden); you cannot dig holes in a porch, a hallway or a driveway."},{"q":"She pushed the twins around the park in a double ______ while she went jogging.","o":["stroller","cradle","playpen","high chair"],"a":0,"e":"A stroller (US) is a small seat on wheels for a baby (UK: pushchair / buggy); a cradle, a playpen and a high chair stay in one place."},{"q":"If you clip this ______ from the Sunday paper, you'll get two dollars off a box of cereal.","o":["coupon","receipt","invoice","refund"],"a":0,"e":"A coupon is a printed ticket that gives you a discount on a product."},{"q":"Put the drinks on my ______; I'll pay for everything when we leave.","o":["tab","tip","menu","receipt"],"a":0,"e":"A tab is a running bill at a bar or restaurant that you pay at the end: 'Put it on my tab.'"},{"q":"The salary isn't great, but the ______ are excellent: health insurance, a pension plan and three weeks of paid leave.","o":["benefits","wages","profits","duties"],"a":0,"e":"Benefits are what a job gives you in addition to pay, such as health insurance and paid leave."},{"q":"Driving in Manhattan is a nightmare, so we took the ______ uptown; the station was right under our hotel.","o":["subway","underpass","freeway","sidewalk"],"a":0,"e":"Subway (US) = underground railway (UK: the Underground). A British 'subway' is a pedestrian underpass."},{"q":"The sign outside the motel said 'No ______,' which meant every room was already taken.","o":["Vacancy","Service","Admission","Parking"],"a":0,"e":"A vacancy is an available room; 'No Vacancy' means the motel is full."},{"q":"The cut on his forehead was so deep that the doctor had to put in six ______.","o":["stitches","splinters","bandages","pills"],"a":0,"e":"Stitches are pieces of thread used to sew a deep cut closed; bandages are put on, not in."},{"q":"You'll need a tetanus *booster* every ten years.","o":["an extra dose of a vaccine","a daily vitamin tablet","a car seat for a small child","a routine blood test"],"a":0,"e":"A booster is an additional dose of a vaccine that keeps the protection strong."},{"q":"After a slow first week, the new recruits are finally ______ steady progress on the rifle range.","o":["making","doing","taking","having"],"a":0,"e":"make progress = improve or move forward; 'do progress' is a common error."},{"q":"Stop making ______ and just tell me why the report wasn't on my desk this morning.","o":["excuses","reasons","motives","pretexts"],"a":0,"e":"make excuses = give reasons, often false ones, to avoid blame."},{"q":"After a night shift at the gate, I usually ______ a short nap before picking up the kids from school.","o":["take","make","do","give"],"a":0,"e":"take a nap = sleep for a short time during the day."},{"q":"The maintenance crew ______ great pride in keeping their aircraft spotless.","o":["takes","makes","does","gives"],"a":0,"e":"take pride in = feel satisfied with and care about something you do."},{"q":"She ______ her employer two weeks' notice before starting her new job in Seattle.","o":["gave","made","did","paid"],"a":0,"e":"give (two weeks') notice = officially tell your employer that you are leaving."},{"q":"Could you ______ an eye on my bag while I buy a ticket?","o":["keep","hold","take","make"],"a":0,"e":"keep an eye on = watch something to make sure it is safe."},{"q":"Our daughter was running a ______ fever, so we took her to the emergency room.","o":["high","tall","strong","big"],"a":0,"e":"a high fever (run a fever = have a fever)."},{"q":"The ______ question on everyone's mind was whether the deployment would be extended.","o":["burning","fiery","flaming","boiling"],"a":0,"e":"a burning question = a very important and urgent question."},{"q":"Since the new fuel system was installed, the ______ of our trucks has improved by almost 20 percent.","o":["efficiency","efficient","efficiently","inefficient"],"a":0,"e":"'the ___ of' needs a noun: efficiency. Efficient is the adjective, efficiently the adverb."},{"q":"Soldiers who fail to ______ on the rifle range this week will have to try again in March.","o":["qualify","qualified","qualification","qualifying"],"a":0,"e":"After 'fail to' we need the base form of the verb: qualify (= reach the required standard)."},{"q":"Repairing the storm damage to the hangar roof will cost a ______ amount of money.","o":["considerable","considerably","consideration","considers"],"a":0,"e":"An adjective is needed before the noun 'amount': considerable (= large). Considerably is the adverb."},{"q":"Corporal Ruiz takes great ______ in keeping her equipment spotless.","o":["pride","proud","proudly","prided"],"a":0,"e":"'take pride in something' uses the noun pride; proud is the adjective (be proud of)."},{"q":"Forecasters expect the storm to ______ overnight before it reaches the coast.","o":["intensify","intense","intensity","intensely"],"a":0,"e":"'expect something to + verb': to intensify (= become stronger)."},{"q":"This small car is very ______; it gets almost 50 miles per gallon on the highway.","o":["economical","economy","economically","economize"],"a":0,"e":"After 'very' we need an adjective: economical (= saving money or fuel)."},{"q":"To avoid being tracked, the radio operator switched to a different ______ every few minutes.","o":["frequency","frequent","frequently","frequenting"],"a":0,"e":"'a different ___' needs a noun: frequency (a radio channel). Frequently is the adverb."},{"q":"Thanks to the ______ of local businesses, every child on base received a holiday gift.","o":["generosity","generous","generously","ungenerous"],"a":0,"e":"'the ___ of' needs a noun: generosity. Generous is the adjective."},{"q":"Regular exercise and a balanced diet are essential for good ______.","o":["health","healthy","healthily","heal"],"a":0,"e":"'for good ___' needs a noun: health. Healthy is the adjective."},{"q":"Since the new gym opened, attendance at morning workouts has ______ by almost a third.","o":["risen","raised","rose","arisen"],"a":0,"e":"Rise / rose / risen has no object (attendance has risen); raise needs an object (raise prices); arise = come into existence (a problem arises)."},{"q":"Before you ship your household goods overseas, ______ them for their full value.","o":["insure","ensure","assure","reassure"],"a":0,"e":"Insure = buy insurance against loss or damage; ensure = make sure something happens; assure = tell someone confidently that something is true."},{"q":"The airline will *compensate* passengers whose bags arrive more than two days late.","o":["repay for their losses","send a written apology to","put on a later flight","give priority service to"],"a":0,"e":"Compensate = give someone money or something else to make up for a loss, injury or trouble."},{"q":"This year's class of interpreters is the most *diverse* the school has ever had.","o":["varied, with many differences","highly skilled and very experienced","larger than in past years","hard to teach and manage"],"a":0,"e":"Diverse = including many different types of people or things."},{"q":"Planting a row of trees along the runway helped *mitigate* the noise for nearby homes.","o":["reduce the effect of","increase the level of","measure accurately","spread more widely"],"a":0,"e":"Mitigate = make something bad less serious or harmful."},{"q":"The editor marked the second paragraph as *redundant* and deleted it from the final report.","o":["unnecessary","incomplete","confusing","out of date"],"a":0,"e":"Redundant = not needed because it repeats something or is more than necessary. (In British English it can also mean 'dismissed from a job'.)"},{"q":"The community college agreed to *waive* the application fee for military families.","o":["not charge","double","refund","publicize"],"a":0,"e":"Waive = officially decide not to demand a payment or apply a rule."},{"q":"The sale of the house is *contingent on* the buyer getting a bank loan.","o":["dependent on","unrelated to","sped up by","delayed by"],"a":0,"e":"Contingent on = depending on something that may or may not happen."},{"q":"The missing generator on the equipment list was simply an *oversight* by the supply clerk.","o":["an unintentional mistake","careful supervision","a deliberate trick","a planned cost-cutting measure"],"a":0,"e":"Oversight = a mistake made because you did not notice something. (It can also mean 'supervision', but not here.)"},{"q":"The new commander promised a more *transparent* process for approving leave requests.","o":["open and honest","able to be seen through","faster and simpler","strict and formal"],"a":0,"e":"Transparent (of a process) = open and honest, so people can see how decisions are made."}]},{"id":"i_idm","sec":"Idioms","title":"American idioms","desc":"Common expressions and their meaning","items":[{"q":"Getting 100 on the ECL would be *a feather in your cap*.","o":["an impossible goal","a worthless task","a proud achievement","an unnoteworthy feat"],"a":2,"e":"a feather in your cap an achievement to be proud of It's a real feather in our cap to be representing Denmark in this contest."},{"q":"This new office furniture *fits the bill*.","o":["is too expensive","is very ugly","meets our needs exactly","is already out-of- style"],"a":2,"e":"If something fits the bill, it is perfect. It's just what you want and need. It meets your needs exactly."},{"q":"I'll try to *keep them at bay* while you get away.","o":["help them","kill them","lend them a boat","hinder them"],"a":3,"e":"hold/keep sth/sb at bay : to hinder or to prevent someone or something unpleasant Exercise can help keep fat at bay."},{"q":"Craig got his next assignment. He'll be *in the boondocks* for three years.","o":["in a nice metropolis","in a remote, primitive place","in his unit's headquarters","in an enviable place that the rest of us"],"a":1,"e":"*The boondocks* is a very remote, primitive area far from big cities. There are no cultural amenities within hundreds of miles."},{"q":"The movie was *terribly good*.","o":["I disliked the movie.","I loathed the movie.","I thought it was awful.","I liked it a lot."],"a":3,"e":"*Terribly* = *awfully*, extremely, quite, very (The key word here is \"good,\" not \"terrible.\")"},{"q":"Let's *stop working on* this exercise for a minute and do something different.","o":["look after","come across","drop out of","put aside"],"a":3,"e":"*Put aside* = move something to the side and not work with it for a while"},{"q":"Can you finish the job by tomorrow? - *no sweat*.","o":["no","probably not","no problem","maybe yes/maybe no"],"a":2,"e":"*No sweat* = It will be so easy that we won't even sweat."},{"q":"My neighbor drives *like a bat out of hell*.","o":["slowly","carefully","very fast","considerately"],"a":2,"e":"*A bat out of hell*= fast, wild, crazy, dangerous"},{"q":"Look at Craig. He's typing *up a storm*, isn't he?","o":["He's making mistakes.","He's angry at us.","He's working very hard.","He's trying not to work."],"a":2,"e":"to do anything *up a storm* means to do it very hard, very seriously, working much job at hand."},{"q":"After a couple of beers, Craig started *spilling his guts*.","o":["telling a lot of secrets","vomiting","laughing at silly jokes","asking to be served a lot of good"],"a":0,"e":"to spill your guts = to tell all of your secrets to confess a lot of serious things"},{"q":"*I sent for* Mariah Carey's new CD.","o":["loaned out","borrowed","ordered by mail","threw out"],"a":2,"e":"*Send for* = to order something through the mail system"},{"q":"You have to *search for* that word in the dictionary.","o":["think up","keep on","send for","look up"],"a":3,"e":"*Look up* = search for in a book, try to find in a book"},{"q":"The tour guide *called our attention to* a lot of old buildings.","o":["got through","stood up","turned up","pointed out"],"a":3,"e":"*Point out* = call attention to = tell people about = show = demonstrate"},{"q":"He *is a candidate for* promotion this month.","o":["is up on","is behind in","us up to","is up for"],"a":3,"e":"*To be up for* = to be a candidate for advancement She is up for soldier of the quarter, and she'll probably get it."},{"q":"Some prisoners have to *subsist on* nothing but bread and water for months.","o":["deal with","keep on","look out for","live on"],"a":3,"e":"*Live on* = to survive on. You live on food. You live on a certain amount of money per month."},{"q":"We Can't *remain at an equal pace with* that car. It's too fast.","o":["drop out of","check up on","get on with","keep up with"],"a":3,"e":"*Keep up with* = maintain the same speed as someone or something else."},{"q":"Some people say President Grant was *crooked*.","o":["honest","beneficent","short","dishonest"],"a":3,"e":"*Crooked* = not straight = slang for dishonest"},{"q":"Report to the Major _____ once!","o":["at","on","in","to"],"a":0,"e":"fixed expression *at* once, meaning without delay, without hesitation"},{"q":"My father disapproves _____ most of my friends.","o":["at","with","to","of"],"a":3,"e":"fixed expression *approve of disapprove of*"},{"q":"Musicians have to spend most of their time _____ the road.","o":["on","in","of","for"],"a":0,"e":"fixed expression Traveling *on* the road by bus or car or van."},{"q":"My country has been involved _____ wars for most of this century.","o":["in","to","at","of"],"a":0,"e":"fixed expression You are *involved in* something."},{"q":"I am very good _____ tennis.","o":["of","at","to","for"],"a":1,"e":"fixed expression You are *good at* something or *bad at* something."},{"q":"My neighbor was convicted _____ car theft.","o":["of","by","with","to"],"a":0,"e":"Fixed expression to be *convicted of* First, he was *charged with* the crime."},{"q":"I am ashamed _____ myself.","o":["of","to","by","for"],"a":0,"e":"fixed expression. Ashamed of. Opposite is proud of."},{"q":"I give up! You are _____ redemption!","o":["around","across","beyond","over"],"a":2,"e":"*Beyond* means past the point of. Fixed expressions: beyond hope, beyond redemption, beyond salvation."},{"q":"If I tell you a secret, will you promise to keep it _____ strictest confidence?","o":["at","of","in","to"],"a":2,"e":"fixed expression to keep *in* confidence"},{"q":"It's time to *hit the hay*.","o":["eat something","start fighting","save money","go to bed"],"a":3,"e":"*Hit the hay* = go to bed. In the old days, people slept on piles of hay."},{"q":"I told you a little white lie.","o":["I fibbed.","I flinched.","I forged.","I framed."],"a":0,"e":"A *little white lie* = a small lie that is not serious = a *fib*."},{"q":"_____ fire, do not try to use the elevators.","o":["In accordance with","In care of","In case of","By means of"],"a":2,"e":"fixed expression meaning \"if it should happen.\" *In case of* rain, the game will be postponed. In case of an emergency, call 911."},{"q":"Craig is going to tie the knot next month. What will Craig do?","o":["get married","fail a test","mail a package","shoot a gun"],"a":0,"e":"\"To tie the knot\" is an idiom meaning to get married."},{"q":"The new mechanic was warned that anyone who doesn't *pull their weight* will be moved to the night shift.","o":["do a fair share of the work","lift heavy parts without help","arrive at work on time","follow every safety rule"],"a":0,"e":"Pull your weight = do your fair share of the work in a team."},{"q":"Before we brief the colonel, let's meet for ten minutes so we're all *on the same page*.","o":["in agreement about the plan","reading the same document","sitting at the same table","assigned to the same office"],"a":0,"e":"On the same page = sharing the same understanding of a situation or agreeing on what to do."},{"q":"He's only been in the unit for a week, so *cut him some slack* if he gets lost on base.","o":["don't be too hard on him","show him a shorter route","report him to his sergeant","lend him your map"],"a":0,"e":"Cut someone some slack = be less strict or critical with someone because of their situation."},{"q":"Lieutenant Moore missed two weeks of planning, so the staff spent the morning bringing her *up to speed*.","o":["informed about the latest details","back to her full physical fitness","ready to lead the convoy at higher speed","in line for an early promotion"],"a":0,"e":"Bring someone up to speed = give someone the latest information so they understand the current situation."},{"q":"When the shipment went missing, every office tried to *pass the buck* instead of solving the problem.","o":["blame another office","pay for the lost cargo","hide the extra money","send the cargo elsewhere"],"a":0,"e":"Pass the buck = shift the responsibility or blame to someone else. (\"The buck stops here\" = I accept final responsibility.)"},{"q":"Sorry I didn't answer your email — I've been *snowed under* since the audit started.","o":["extremely busy with work","stuck at home by bad weather","feeling sick and tired","away from the office on leave"],"a":0,"e":"Snowed under = having so much work that you can hardly deal with it."},{"q":"If you wait until December to book your flight home, you'll *pay through the nose* for it.","o":["pay a very high price","pay in monthly installments","pay with airline miles","pay only at the airport"],"a":0,"e":"Pay through the nose = pay much more than something should cost."},{"q":"We've been *pinching pennies* all year so we can afford a trip to see my parents in Ohio.","o":["spending as little as possible","working extra shifts on weekends","borrowing money from friends","applying for a bank loan"],"a":0,"e":"Pinch pennies = be very careful with money and spend as little as possible."},{"q":"The base bowling alley has been *in the red* for three years, so it may close next spring.","o":["losing money","very popular","being repainted","under investigation"],"a":0,"e":"In the red = losing money or in debt. The opposite is \"in the black\" (making a profit)."},{"q":"I'd love to join you on the ski trip, but I'm *short of money* until payday.","o":["strapped for cash","rolling in dough","made of money","sitting on a gold mine"],"a":0,"e":"Strapped for cash = having very little money at the moment. (Rolling in dough / made of money = very rich.)"},{"q":"Three restaurants near the main gate *went out of business* during the pandemic.","o":["went belly up","went the extra mile","went Dutch","went with the flow"],"a":0,"e":"Go belly up = fail completely; go bankrupt (like a dead fish floating upside down)."},{"q":"The deal to keep the factory open was signed *at the last possible moment*, only hours before the deadline.","o":["at the eleventh hour","around the clock","at the drop of a hat","once in a blue moon"],"a":0,"e":"At the eleventh hour = at the last possible moment before a deadline."},{"q":"Our flight was delayed four hours, so we *killed time* by walking around the airport shops.","o":["passed the time while waiting","spent too much money","complained to the airline staff","rushed to find another flight"],"a":0,"e":"Kill time = do something to make the time pass while you wait."},{"q":"We can't afford new radios this year, but we might upgrade them *down the road*.","o":["in the future","at a shop nearby","during the convoy","immediately"],"a":0,"e":"Down the road = at some time in the future."},{"q":"The rear guard's mission was to slow the enemy down and *gain extra time* for the main column to withdraw.","o":["buy time","kill time","make time","do time"],"a":0,"e":"Buy time = delay something so that you have more time. (Kill time = pass time while waiting; make time = find time for something; do time = serve a prison sentence.)"},{"q":"Getting a slot at Ranger School this year is *a long shot*, but Private Hale plans to apply anyway.","o":["a slim chance","a shooting test","a distant post","a sure thing"],"a":0,"e":"A long shot = something that has only a small chance of succeeding."},{"q":"When you can't decide between two good job offers, sometimes you just have to *go with your gut*.","o":["trust your instincts","ask for more money","eat before deciding","follow your boss's advice"],"a":0,"e":"Go with your gut = follow your instinct or feeling instead of long analysis."},{"q":"Free college tuition in exchange for two more years of service? For me, that was *a no-brainer*.","o":["an easy decision","a foolish mistake","a difficult choice","a crazy idea"],"a":0,"e":"A no-brainer = a decision so easy and obvious that you hardly need to think about it."},{"q":"Captain Wells had planned to retire, but she *had a change of heart* and signed up for another tour.","o":["changed her mind","had heart surgery","felt very sad","lost her courage"],"a":0,"e":"Have a change of heart = change your opinion or decision about something."},{"q":"The weather forecast was uncertain, but the commander decided to *be extra careful* and cancel the night jump.","o":["err on the side of caution","throw caution to the wind","push his luck","play devil's advocate"],"a":0,"e":"Err on the side of caution = choose the safer option when you are not sure. (Throw caution to the wind = take a big risk.)"}]},{"id":"i_pv","sec":"Idioms","title":"Phrasal verbs","desc":"Make up, pick up, put aside...","items":[{"q":"My date *stood me up* last night.","o":["took me dancing","didn't even show up","brought me flowers and candy","showed me a great time"],"a":1,"e":"stand sb up: to intentionally fail to meet someone when you said you would, especially I don't know if I've been stood up or if she's just late - I'll wait another half hour."},{"q":"That song really *recalls* good memories of when I lived with my grandmother.","o":["brings back","cheers up","thinks over","turns over"],"a":0,"e":"*Bring back* = to make you remember something from the past. It brings a memory back to your brain."},{"q":"Don't *ridicule* other people's mistakes in class.","o":["laugh at","cheer up","look up to","bring about"],"a":0,"e":"*Laugh at* = make fun of = ridicule = deride"},{"q":"You should *review* this vocabulary list before we take the test.","o":["do over","go over","be over","send over"],"a":1,"e":"go over = review = look at again = study"},{"q":"I cannot *accept* any additional duties at this time.","o":["take on","get across","bring back","stand by"],"a":0,"e":"*Take on* = accept, agree to perform extra work"},{"q":"*Carefully consider all the details* before you do it.","o":["Get it across","Think it through","Come over it","Take it back"],"a":1,"e":"phrasal verb think through = carefully consider everything in advance"},{"q":"Please *submit your paper* before 2:35.","o":["look into it","send for it","report it in","turn it in"],"a":3,"e":"*Turn in* = to hand in = to submit = to give something to someone after completing it"},{"q":"*Increase* the volume. I can't hear anything.","o":["turn down","turn off","turn over","turn up"],"a":3,"e":"*Turn up* = increase volume = make it louder"},{"q":"It's hot now. I think I'll *store* all my sweaters for the summer.","o":["put away","take out","drop out","keep on"],"a":0,"e":"*Put away* = put something in storage, put something in a different place for later use."},{"q":"Before you buy that coat, you should *determine it if fits well*.","o":["try it out","do it over","try it on","check it off"],"a":2,"e":"*Try on* = to put clothing on to check the fit"},{"q":"We *expected him to come* for an hour before we finally left without him.","o":["waited for him","dropped him off","thought him up","made him over"],"a":0,"e":"*Wait for* = not leave until someone arrives = expect someone to arrive"},{"q":"When you get things at the store, *mark those items on the list*.","o":["check them off","check them out","check them in","check up on them"],"a":0,"e":"*Check something off* = to mark items on a list to show that you have taken care of them."},{"q":"I will not *tolerate* any more cheating on the tests!","o":["try on","put up with","remind of","part with"],"a":1,"e":"*Put up with* = tolerate = allow to happen"},{"q":"When will the boss be able to *inspect* the new equipment?","o":["look out","be up on","check out","see off"],"a":2,"e":"*Check out* = to look at something = to inspect = to see how something is"},{"q":"The Commander *reprimanded* Capt. Barrow during formation.","o":["called down","called on","called for","called in"],"a":0,"e":"reprimand = call down = scold = give a tongue-lashing to= chew out"},{"q":"Nothing will _____ him from finishing the race.","o":["prevent","avoid","refuse","deny"],"a":0,"e":"*Prevent from* is the correct pattern. *Avoid* is not followed by *from*."},{"q":"When the dog started growling, the delivery driver slowly *backed off* and left the package at the gate.","o":["moved away","shouted at it","fell over","ran toward it"],"a":0,"e":"back off = move back or away from someone or something."},{"q":"The security camera footage *bore out* the guard's account of what happened at the gate.","o":["confirmed","contradicted","replaced","delayed"],"a":0,"e":"bear out (bore out) = show that something is true; confirm."},{"q":"Jenna ______ her frustration for months until she finally exploded at a staff meeting.","o":["bottled up","backed up","made up","took up"],"a":0,"e":"bottle up = hide strong feelings for a long time."},{"q":"If you want to pass the language exam in June, you'll have to *buckle down* and study every evening.","o":["work hard","take it easy","find a tutor","skip some classes"],"a":0,"e":"buckle down = start working hard and seriously."},{"q":"The roof of the old warehouse *caved in* under the weight of the heavy snow.","o":["collapsed","leaked","was repaired","shook"],"a":0,"e":"cave in = fall down or inward; collapse."},{"q":"I think I'm *coming down with* a cold; my throat has been sore all day.","o":["starting to get","getting over","worried about","protected from"],"a":0,"e":"come down with = become sick with an illness."},{"q":"The doctor told him to *cut back on* coffee and get more sleep.","o":["drink less","drink more","stop buying","switch to"],"a":0,"e":"cut back on = reduce the amount of something."},{"q":"When the food arrived, the hungry soldiers *dug in* without waiting for the speeches to end.","o":["started eating","complained","sat down quietly","paid the bill"],"a":0,"e":"dig in (informal) = start eating eagerly."},{"q":"Before the move, we *made* a list of everything that needed to be packed.","o":["drew up","drew on","drew back","drew in"],"a":0,"e":"draw up a list = write a list (draw on = use your experience or resources)."},{"q":"Rising fuel prices are *eating into* the trucking company's profits.","o":["reducing","increasing","protecting","measuring"],"a":0,"e":"eat into = use up or reduce part of something, such as money or time."},{"q":"Use a rake to ______ the gravel before you lay the paving stones.","o":["even out","knock out","give out","cut out"],"a":0,"e":"even out = make a surface flat and level."},{"q":"The storm *gradually lost its strength* before it reached the coast.","o":["fizzled out","fizzled up","broke out","flared up"],"a":0,"e":"fizzle out = slowly become weaker and end."},{"q":"Most units ______ soldiers who show up late to formation, even by a minute.","o":["frown on","look up to","stand by","go along with"],"a":0,"e":"frown on = think that something or someone's behavior is wrong."},{"q":"At the end of my shift, I ______ the keys and the logbook to the next guard.","o":["handed over","handed down","took over","got over"],"a":0,"e":"hand over = pass something or responsibility to another person."},{"q":"The two departments met on Monday to *iron out* their differences over the new schedule.","o":["settle","discover","increase","report"],"a":0,"e":"iron out = solve small problems or differences."},{"q":"The plant *laid off* nearly half its workers when orders from the Army dropped.","o":["dismissed","hired","trained","promoted"],"a":0,"e":"lay off = end workers' jobs because there is not enough work."},{"q":"The aircraft climbed to 30,000 feet and then *began to fly horizontally*.","o":["leveled off","leveled up","took off","touched down"],"a":0,"e":"level off = (of an aircraft) stop climbing and fly level."},{"q":"Our rations were delayed by the storm, so the platoon had to *make do with* crackers and canned fruit for two days.","o":["manage with","complain about","pay extra for","give away"],"a":0,"e":"make do with = manage with what is available, even if it is not ideal."},{"q":"Many travelers *miss out on* cheaper fares because they book their flights at the last minute.","o":["fail to get","complain about","pay less for","ask about"],"a":0,"e":"miss out on = lose the chance to get or enjoy something."},{"q":"The interpreter *noted down* every number the caller gave so she could repeat it accurately.","o":["wrote down","forgot","questioned","translated"],"a":0,"e":"note down = make a written note of something."},{"q":"Despite her strong record, Captain Ortiz was *passed over* for the command position in favor of a less experienced officer.","o":["not selected","recommended","considered first","sent overseas"],"a":0,"e":"be passed over (for) = not be chosen when you expected to be."},{"q":"The risky decision *proved successful*: the small company's app now has over a million users.","o":["paid off","paid back","fell through","broke down"],"a":0,"e":"pay off = succeed. fall through = fail to happen; break down = stop working."},{"q":"Technicians spent all morning trying to *pin down* the cause of the radar failure.","o":["identify exactly","repair quickly","hide from the boss","explain to others"],"a":0,"e":"pin down = find out or identify something exactly."},{"q":"Bad weather has *pushed back* the parachute jump to Thursday afternoon.","o":["delayed","canceled","moved earlier","shortened"],"a":0,"e":"push back = postpone, move to a later time."},{"q":"After a twenty-minute fight, my father finally ______ a huge catfish at Lake Texoma.","o":["reeled in","reeled off","rolled in","let off"],"a":0,"e":"reel in = pull a fish toward you by winding the line. reel off = say a list quickly."},{"q":"With her strong math background, Jana ______ the navigation course while others struggled.","o":["sailed through","sailed off","fell behind","went off"],"a":0,"e":"sail through = do something successfully and easily."},{"q":"After a suspicious package was found, MPs ______ the parking lot and called the bomb squad.","o":["sealed off","sealed in","set off","showed off"],"a":0,"e":"seal off = close an area. set off = cause to explode."},{"q":"The battalion will *ship out* to Germany at the end of the month.","o":["leave for duty overseas","be inspected by officers","return home","receive supplies"],"a":0,"e":"ship out = leave, especially to go overseas on military duty."},{"q":"The new platoon leader took a few days to *size up* her soldiers before making any changes.","o":["judge","measure for uniforms","promote","replace"],"a":0,"e":"size up = observe and form an opinion of."},{"q":"The flooding *spread* into the neighboring county, closing several roads.","o":["spilled over","spelled out","passed over","turned over"],"a":0,"e":"spill over = spread beyond limits. spell out = explain clearly."},{"q":"Drink plenty of water and rest in the shade to ______ heat exhaustion during the march.","o":["stave off","stand off","set off","start off"],"a":0,"e":"stave off = prevent. set off = cause something to start."},{"q":"The colonel *swore in* twenty new recruits in front of their proud families.","o":["gave the oath to","shouted angrily at","trained","welcomed home"],"a":0,"e":"swear in = officially admit someone by having them take an oath."},{"q":"Marshals spent three years trying to *locate* the escaped prisoner.","o":["track down","back down","lay down","settle down"],"a":0,"e":"track down = locate. back down = stop insisting; settle down = become calm."},{"q":"The factory will *gradually reduce* production over the next year before it closes for good.","o":["wind down","write down","break down","back down"],"a":0,"e":"wind down = reduce gradually before ending. break down = stop working."}]},{"id":"l_mix","sec":"Listening","title":"Listening","desc":"Recorded American voices, 5 question types","items":[{"id":"L01","k":"s","L":[["M","The flight to San Antonio leaves at fourteen fifteen, not at four fifteen.","L01-1.mp3?v=2ab4893d10"]],"q":"When does the flight leave?","o":["At 2:15 in the afternoon","At 4:15 in the afternoon","At 4:50 in the morning","At 2:50 in the afternoon"],"a":0,"e":"In military time, fourteen fifteen (1415) is 2:15 p.m. The speaker corrects the mistake \"four fifteen\"."},{"id":"L1760","k":"s","L":[["M","The ferry runs every forty-five minutes, and the first one leaves at six.","L1760-1.mp3?v=9931086596"]],"q":"When does the second ferry leave?","o":["At 6:45","At 6:15","At 7:00","At 6:30"],"a":0,"e":"Forty-five minutes after six is 6:45."},{"id":"L1908","k":"s","L":[["M","Our team has to finish the bridge before the rainy season begins.","L1908-1.mp3?v=68a6a3b99c"]],"q":"What is the deadline for the bridge?","o":["The start of the rainy season","The end of the rainy season","Next year","There is no deadline."],"a":0,"e":"They must finish before the rain starts."},{"id":"L2048","k":"s","L":[["W","The shoe store is closing, so everything is seventy percent off.","L2048-1.mp3?v=b8ab9c3b27"]],"q":"Why are prices low?","o":["The store is going out of business.","The shoes are damaged.","It is the end of summer.","The store just opened."],"a":0,"e":"A closing sale lowers prices."},{"id":"L2191","k":"s","L":[["M","I paid top dollar for these boots, and they started falling apart after just two weeks in the field.","L2191-1.mp3?v=917aab1fad"]],"q":"What is the man complaining about?","o":["Expensive footwear wore out quickly.","The boots cost only one dollar.","He lost his boots in the field.","The boots took two weeks to arrive."],"a":0,"e":"He paid a high price, yet the boots fell apart very soon."},{"id":"L2367","k":"s","L":[["M","The town's only hospital is building a new wing for children.","L2367-1.mp3?v=1bb4d813c8"]],"q":"What is the hospital building?","o":["A children's wing","A parking garage","A new hospital in another town","An emergency room for adults"],"a":0,"e":"It is adding a wing for children."},{"id":"L2616","k":"s","L":[["M","Pack your carry-on so that the laptop comes out easily; security will ask you to put it in a separate bin.","L2616-1.mp3?v=408af86470"]],"q":"Why does the man give this advice?","o":["Computers must be screened on their own.","Laptops are not allowed in carry-on bags.","The bins at security are very small.","Security usually keeps the laptops."],"a":0,"e":"Security will want the laptop in its own bin, so it should be easy to take out."},{"id":"L2739","k":"s","L":[["W","The dining facility serves breakfast until eight, but on weekends brunch runs from nine to one, and there's no separate lunch.","L2739-1.mp3?v=e7e21ed9b2"]],"q":"What can be concluded about weekend meals?","o":["Morning and midday meals are combined.","Breakfast is served until eight.","Lunch starts at one o'clock.","There is no meal before noon."],"a":0,"e":"On weekends, brunch replaces both breakfast and lunch."},{"id":"L2861","k":"s","L":[["W","I accidentally deleted the file, but luckily I found it in the recycle bin and restored it.","L2861-1.mp3?v=ba32165fc6"]],"q":"What happened to the file?","o":["It was recovered.","It was lost forever.","It was recycled into a new file.","It was sent by mistake."],"a":0,"e":"She restored the deleted file from the recycle bin, so she got it back."},{"id":"L2984","k":"s","L":[["M","The turkey needs about four hours in the oven, so if we want to eat at six, it has to go in by two.","L2984-1.mp3?v=6147f2b37c"]],"q":"When must the turkey start cooking?","o":["No later than two o'clock.","No later than four o'clock.","No earlier than six o'clock.","No later than ten o'clock."],"a":0,"e":"Four hours before six o'clock is two o'clock, so it must be in the oven by then."},{"id":"L03","k":"r","L":[["M","How long have you been stationed at this base?","L03-1.mp3?v=f27ddd406c"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["Since last March.","At the main gate.","By bus, every morning.","About ten miles from here."],"a":0,"e":"\"How long\" asks about a period of time. \"Since last March\" gives the start of that period."},{"id":"L1229","k":"r","L":[["M","I heard they're bringing in a new instructor for the driver training course. Is that right?","L1229-1.mp3?v=4d4c2f42f5"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["Yes, she's supposed to start Monday.","Turn right just past the training center.","I didn't hear you come in.","I drove there by myself."],"a":0,"e":"She confirms the news and says when the new instructor begins."},{"id":"L1354","k":"r","L":[["W","How long did it take you to get used to sleeping outdoors during field training?","L1354-1.mp3?v=d18dac63d7"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["To be honest, I never did.","I used to camp outdoors a lot.","It takes two hours to get there.","The field is a mile long."],"a":0,"e":"He means he never got used to it at all."},{"id":"L1470","k":"r","L":[["W","Can you show me how to use the new radio?","L1470-1.mp3?v=2cd66469b2"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["Sure, it's easier than the old one.","The new radio is lighter.","I used the radio yesterday.","Radios are expensive."],"a":0,"e":"The answer agrees."},{"id":"L1597","k":"r","L":[["M","What do you do in your free time?","L1597-1.mp3?v=90ad5619ef"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["I like to read and go fishing.","I have free time on weekends.","My time is very free.","I work from nine to five."],"a":0,"e":"The question asks for activities."},{"id":"L2484","k":"r","L":[["W","Aren't you going to try out for the basketball team this season?","L2484-1.mp3?v=7c0e3d79ed"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["Not with my schedule. Maybe next year.","I tried on a few, but none fit.","The season starts in April.","They won their last three games."],"a":0,"e":"He is too busy to join now but may do it later."},{"id":"L3200","k":"r","L":[["M","Wasn't the staff meeting supposed to start at ten? Nobody's here yet.","L3200-1.mp3?v=3567c87cf7"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["It was moved to eleven. Didn't you hear?","Yes, I started working here ten years ago.","The staff sergeant isn't here today.","I'm supposed to meet her at the gate."],"a":0,"e":"She explains that the meeting was rescheduled for a later time."},{"id":"L3297","k":"r","L":[["W","Could you tell me which bus goes downtown? This map is really confusing.","L3297-1.mp3?v=7adf1e3fb2"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["Any of the blue ones will get you there.","Sure, I'll tell him when I see him.","The downtown area is very crowded.","I bought that map at the gas station by the gate."],"a":0,"e":"He tells her that all the blue buses go downtown."},{"id":"L3393","k":"r","L":[["W","Do you know if the base pool is open to family members on weekends?","L3393-1.mp3?v=4417e86472"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["As long as they show their ID cards.","My family usually visits on weekends.","I swam about twenty laps this morning.","I don't know any of the members."],"a":0,"e":"He says family members may use the pool if they have identification."},{"id":"L3490","k":"r","L":[["M","They're calling for thunderstorms all weekend. Do you still want to go camping at the lake?","L3490-1.mp3?v=db64445c0e"]],"q":"Choose the best answer.","o":["Not unless the forecast changes.","I called you twice over the weekend.","The lake is about an hour north of here.","We went camping there last summer."],"a":0,"e":"She means she does not want to go if the bad weather is still expected."},{"id":"L04","k":"d","L":[["W","Are you coming to the briefing at zero eight hundred?","L04-1.mp3?v=ccc6d507f8"],["M","I wouldn't miss it for the world.","L04-2.mp3?v=c18f292fb1"]],"q":"What does the man mean?","o":["He will certainly go to the briefing.","He does not want to go to the briefing.","He has never been to a briefing.","He thinks the briefing is too early."],"a":0,"e":"\"I wouldn't miss it for the world\" means \"I will certainly be there.\""},{"id":"L514","k":"d","L":[["M","I'd like to sign out a laptop for the staff meeting tomorrow.","L514-1.mp3?v=7dce88dc89"],["W","I can do that, but it has to be back on my desk by sixteen hundred.","L514-2.mp3?v=3d41b9f828"]],"q":"What does the woman tell the man?","o":["He must return it by four in the afternoon.","He can keep it for the whole week.","He has to return it by six o'clock.","He needs to bring it to a meeting at four."],"a":0,"e":"Sixteen hundred is military time for 4:00 p.m."},{"id":"L705","k":"d","L":[["M","What's the matter? You look pale.","L705-1.mp3?v=32b9a49d83"],["W","I think I ate something bad at lunch.","L705-2.mp3?v=26b0cdbf9d"]],"q":"What is the woman's problem?","o":["She feels sick from her lunch.","She is very tired.","She is cold.","She is nervous."],"a":0,"e":"She suspects bad food."},{"id":"L897","k":"d","L":[["W","How much do I owe you for the tickets?","L897-1.mp3?v=98c3b26b17"],["M","Nothing; they were free from work.","L897-2.mp3?v=010be04f87"]],"q":"Why doesn't the woman have to pay?","o":["His job gave him the tickets.","He paid for them with his own money.","She already paid him last week.","The show was canceled."],"a":0,"e":"The tickets were free from the man's work, so she owes nothing."},{"id":"L2463","k":"d","L":[["W","Our heating bill was almost double last month's.","L2463-1.mp3?v=f95c0e737a"],["M","No wonder. Somebody left the upstairs window open all weekend while we were away.","L2463-2.mp3?v=c2240e1cce"]],"q":"Why was the bill so high?","o":["Heat was escaping from the house.","The heater was broken all weekend.","They used more electricity upstairs.","They were billed for two months."],"a":0,"e":"An open window over the weekend let the heat out, so they paid more."},{"id":"L3663","k":"d","L":[["W","I opened a new bank account. How long does it take to switch my direct deposit?","L3663-1.mp3?v=6b4da169bd"],["M","If you update it online before the fifteenth, it should take effect on the next payday. Otherwise, it'll be the one after.","L3663-2.mp3?v=0922d3afee"]],"q":"What determines when the change takes effect?","o":["When she submits the change","Which bank she opens it with","How much money she deposits","Whether she goes in person"],"a":0,"e":"An update made before the fifteenth works on the next payday; a later one waits a payday longer."},{"id":"L3776","k":"d","L":[["M","Do I have to fill up the rental before I bring it back tomorrow?","L3776-1.mp3?v=d03694f935"],["W","You don't have to, but if they fill it for you, it's almost nine dollars a gallon.","L3776-2.mp3?v=3dc0560f8b"]],"q":"What does the woman imply?","o":["Refueling it himself would be cheaper.","The car must be returned today.","The gas station is nine miles away.","The rental already has a full tank."],"a":0,"e":"The rental company charges a very high price for fuel, so filling it himself saves money."},{"id":"L3888","k":"d","L":[["M","Doc put me on a temporary profile for my back. Does that mean I'm off PT completely?","L3888-1.mp3?v=59d6a1b1e1"],["W","Not at all. You'll just do whatever the profile allows, like walking or the stationary bike, while everyone else runs.","L3888-2.mp3?v=9f29820387"]],"q":"What does the woman say about the man's physical training?","o":["He will do a modified workout.","He is excused from all workouts.","He must run along with everyone.","He needs a new profile first."],"a":0,"e":"He still does PT, but only the exercises his profile permits, such as walking or biking."},{"id":"L4001","k":"d","L":[["W","Did you get your car back from the body shop?","L4001-1.mp3?v=a396e711a9"],["M","Yesterday, finally. They matched the paint so well you can't even tell where the dent was.","L4001-2.mp3?v=84356d33a6"]],"q":"How does the man feel about the repair?","o":["He is happy with the work.","The paint does not match.","The dent is still visible.","The shop finished too early."],"a":0,"e":"The repair is so good that the damage cannot be seen."},{"id":"L4114","k":"d","L":[["M","Thanks for covering my shift on Friday so I could go to my sister's graduation. I owe you one.","L4114-1.mp3?v=9da3d850a5"],["W","Don't mention it. You can return the favor when my parents visit next month.","L4114-2.mp3?v=1d8d600439"]],"q":"What does the woman expect?","o":["That he'll help her out later","That he'll pay her for Friday","That he'll come to her graduation","That her parents will visit Friday"],"a":0,"e":"She expects him to work for her when her parents come next month."},{"id":"L62","k":"c","L":[["W","My flight gets in at nine forty tonight. Could you pick me up at the airport?","L62-1.mp3?v=8f38737809"],["M","Sure, but I'm on duty until ten. Is ten thirty all right?","L62-2.mp3?v=51e95498bd"],["W","That's fine. It always takes a while to get my bags anyway.","L62-3.mp3?v=bb53b339fe"],["M","Great. I'll meet you outside the baggage claim area.","L62-4.mp3?v=ad380f9f5b"]],"q":"At what time will the man pick the woman up?","o":["At 10:30 p.m.","At 9:40 p.m.","At 10:00 p.m.","At 10:40 p.m."],"a":0,"e":"The man is \"on duty until ten\", so he offers \"ten thirty\", and the woman says \"That's fine.\" Nine forty is when her flight lands."},{"id":"L186","k":"c","L":[["M","Welcome to Fort Hood. How can I help you?","L186-1.mp3?v=42a19c7a7b"],["W","I'm here to visit my son. He's in the First Cavalry.","L186-2.mp3?v=354690d59a"],["M","I'll need to see your ID and his unit information.","L186-3.mp3?v=496677251b"],["W","Here's my license and his address.","L186-4.mp3?v=c452da65b4"]],"q":"Why did the woman come to Fort Hood?","o":["To visit her son","To start a new job","To join the Army","To deliver a package"],"a":0,"e":"She is visiting her son."},{"id":"L258","k":"c","L":[["M","Do you know how to use the new GPS units?","L258-1.mp3?v=517d355f99"],["W","I took the class last week.","L258-2.mp3?v=454852044f"],["M","Can you teach my squad?","L258-3.mp3?v=7f6eca2f64"],["W","Sure, how about Thursday morning?","L258-4.mp3?v=6d5aababa1"]],"q":"Why does the man ask the woman to teach his squad?","o":["She has already been trained on the equipment.","His squad missed last Thursday's morning class.","She is going to teach a GPS class next week.","His own GPS unit stopped working last week."],"a":0,"e":"She took the GPS class last week, so she knows how to use the new units."},{"id":"L342","k":"c","L":[["W","We're going camping this weekend. Want to come?","L342-1.mp3?v=dc81437eb9"],["M","I'd love to, but I don't have a tent.","L342-2.mp3?v=9523239fdf"],["W","You can share ours; it sleeps four.","L342-3.mp3?v=74f57a3e71"],["M","Great, then count me in.","L342-4.mp3?v=9cd3baf986"]],"q":"What will the man do?","o":["Go camping and share their tent","Buy a tent","Stay home","Rent a cabin"],"a":0,"e":"He accepts their offer."},{"id":"L4144","k":"c","L":[["M","We only received half the ammunition we requested for next week's qualification.","L4144-1.mp3?v=9631c5f961"],["W","Half? We've got sixty soldiers who need to qualify.","L4144-2.mp3?v=987423d238"],["M","I know. Ammunition supply says the rest won't be available until the next quarter.","L4144-3.mp3?v=337e62e052"],["W","Then let's put the soldiers whose qualification expires first at the top of the list. The others can wait.","L4144-4.mp3?v=1ec58ab497"]],"q":"How does the woman plan to deal with the shortage?","o":["By deciding who needs to shoot most urgently","By borrowing ammunition from another unit","By canceling next week's qualification","By ordering more for the next quarter"],"a":0,"e":"She will give priority to the soldiers whose qualification runs out soonest."},{"id":"L4185","k":"c","L":[["W","I just tried to book a room at the lodging on post for my school next month. They're completely full.","L4185-1.mp3?v=670e97e9a1"],["M","Did they give you a non-availability number?","L4185-2.mp3?v=242e43f844"],["W","A what?","L4185-3.mp3?v=17017ebbe4"],["M","A number that proves they had no rooms. Without it, finance won't pay for a hotel off post. Call them back and ask for one.","L4185-4.mp3?v=5500548bb0"]],"q":"What does the woman need to do?","o":["Get a reference number from base lodging","Book a hotel room off post right away","Ask finance to find her a room","Change the dates of her school"],"a":0,"e":"She needs the non-availability number so finance will pay for a hotel off post."},{"id":"L4225","k":"c","L":[["W","The fumes from the paint shop are coming into our office through the air vents.","L4225-1.mp3?v=fc6aef3fdb"],["M","I smelled it too. A couple of people have already complained of headaches.","L4225-2.mp3?v=8e66a489a0"],["W","We can't work in here like this. Let's move to the empty classroom across the street until they finish.","L4225-3.mp3?v=a0c46b6a13"],["M","I'll let everyone know, and I'll ask the paint shop how long they'll be at it.","L4225-4.mp3?v=14f8637460"]],"q":"What do the speakers decide to do?","o":["Work in another building for a while","Close all the air vents in the office","Ask the paint shop to stop working","Send the sick people to the clinic"],"a":0,"e":"They will move to the empty classroom across the street until the painting is done."},{"id":"L4265","k":"c","L":[["W","Have you gotten your flu shot yet this year?","L4265-1.mp3?v=af2e0b7e0d"],["M","Not yet. I keep meaning to make an appointment, but I never get around to it.","L4265-2.mp3?v=88a4802228"],["W","You don't need one. The clinic has walk-in hours on Tuesdays and Thursdays from one to four. I was in and out in fifteen minutes.","L4265-3.mp3?v=d9587f8ce0"],["M","Really? Then I'll stop by on Thursday after lunch.","L4265-4.mp3?v=bae66bca30"]],"q":"What did the man not realize?","o":["No appointment is required","The clinic is closed on Thursdays","He had already received the shot","The shot takes fifteen minutes to work"],"a":0,"e":"She tells him he doesn't need an appointment because the clinic has walk-in hours."},{"id":"L4306","k":"c","L":[["M","Your sister's wedding is outdoors on Saturday, right? Have you seen the forecast?","L4306-1.mp3?v=aedd5eace9"],["W","Seventy percent chance of rain. She's been in tears all morning.","L4306-2.mp3?v=c7ab45b20c"],["M","Doesn't the farm have a barn they could use?","L4306-3.mp3?v=8fbd4c8b10"],["W","It's booked for another event. But my uncle rents out party tents, and he's bringing a big one Friday night, just in case.","L4306-4.mp3?v=c891e5c3bd"],["M","Well, that's a relief. At least the guests will stay dry.","L4306-5.mp3?v=48d4bccafc"]],"q":"How will the rain problem probably be solved?","o":["A relative is providing shelter","The wedding will move into a barn","The wedding will be postponed","The guests will bring umbrellas"],"a":0,"e":"Her uncle is bringing a large tent in case it rains."},{"id":"L5014","k":"c","L":[["M","For the after-action review, what do you think went wrong yesterday?","L5014-1.mp3?v=1e8b3f7332"],["W","The plan itself was fine. The problem was that second platoon never heard we'd moved the meeting point.","L5014-2.mp3?v=0b1065961c"],["M","I sent that change to their platoon sergeant.","L5014-3.mp3?v=e7078f5ab5"],["W","Right, but he was out checking vehicles, and nobody passed it on. From now on, we should send changes to at least two people and have them confirm they got it.","L5014-4.mp3?v=706ba7123c"]],"q":"According to the woman, what was the main problem?","o":["A message was never passed along","The meeting point was badly chosen","The plan was too complicated to follow","The platoon sergeant gave the wrong orders"],"a":0,"e":"Second platoon never learned that the meeting point had changed because the information stopped with one person."},{"id":"L59","k":"k","L":[["W","Attention, please. The eleven forty train to Washington will leave from Track Six today, not from Track Two. Because of work on the tracks, the train is running about fifteen minutes behind schedule. We apologize for the delay.","L59-1.mp3?v=839f1b9b27"]],"q":"Which track will the Washington train leave from?","o":["Track 6","Track 2","Track 11","Track 15"],"a":0,"e":"The train \"will leave from Track Six today, not from Track Two.\" Eleven forty is the time of the train, and fifteen minutes is the delay."},{"id":"L976","k":"k","L":[["W","Attention, shoppers. For the next hour, all frozen foods are twenty percent off. This offer is good only until three o'clock, so hurry to aisle twelve and take advantage of these savings.","L976-1.mp3?v=84417372fd"]],"q":"What time is it probably now?","o":["About two o'clock","Just after three","Around noon","Twelve o'clock"],"a":0,"e":"The sale lasts for the next hour and ends at three, so it is about two now."},{"id":"L1021","k":"k","L":[["M","Honeybees are important to farmers because they carry pollen from flower to flower. This helps plants produce fruit and seeds. Without bees, many of the foods we eat would become rare and expensive.","L1021-1.mp3?v=9cf6248486"]],"q":"Why are honeybees important to farmers?","o":["They help plants produce fruit.","They make honey for farmers to sell.","They kill harmful insects.","They improve the soil."],"a":0,"e":"Pollination helps plants produce fruit."},{"id":"L1061","k":"k","L":[["M","Benjamin Franklin was a writer, scientist, and diplomat. He is famous for his experiments with electricity, including flying a kite in a thunderstorm. He also helped write the Declaration of Independence.","L1061-1.mp3?v=7191de0260"]],"q":"What does the speaker say about the kite?","o":["It was part of a scientific test","It was a gift to a diplomat","It was used to send messages","It was flown on a sunny day"],"a":0,"e":"Franklin flew the kite in a thunderstorm as one of his experiments with electricity."},{"id":"L1128","k":"k","L":[["W","Hi, this is Helen from the bank. Your new debit card has been mailed and should arrive within five business days. Please activate it by calling the number on the sticker.","L1128-1.mp3?v=ba39aee950"]],"q":"What is the main reason for Helen's call?","o":["To say a card is on its way","To ask for a new mailing address","To explain why a card was blocked","To report five missing payments"],"a":0,"e":"Helen says the new debit card has been mailed and should arrive soon."},{"id":"L4358","k":"k","L":[["M","Today you'll go through the vehicle rollover trainer. The crew compartment will turn on its side and then upside down, so secure everything loose before we start, including water bottles and phones. Keep your seat belt fastened until the vehicle stops moving completely. When it stops, the vehicle commander will call out, and each person will answer with a status. Then brace yourself with one hand, release the belt with the other, and exit through the nearest door.","L4358-1.mp3?v=6552a64cbd"]],"q":"What must happen right after the vehicle stops moving?","o":["The crew members report on their condition","Everyone unfastens the belt and gets out","Each soldier collects the loose water bottles","The commander leaves through the nearest door"],"a":0,"e":"When the vehicle stops, the commander calls out and each person answers with a status before anyone gets out."},{"id":"L4390","k":"k","L":[["M","Before you leave for the four-day weekend, a few rules. Anyone traveling more than two hundred and fifty miles from post needs an approved leave form, not just a pass. Get at least seven hours of sleep before any long drive, and stop every two hours. If you've been drinking, call a friend, a taxi, or your squad leader, any time of day or night. Formation is Tuesday at zero six thirty, and everyone will be there on time.","L4390-1.mp3?v=6b3e87abb2"]],"q":"What is required of soldiers who plan to travel far from post?","o":["They need formal permission to take leave.","They must stop every two hundred miles.","They must call their squad leader daily.","They must sleep seven hours every day."],"a":0,"e":"Soldiers going more than two hundred and fifty miles away need an approved leave form, not a pass."},{"id":"L4423","k":"k","L":[["W","Hi, Daniel, this is Karen from Westside Auto calling about your car. We finished the brake job this morning, but while it was up on the lift, our mechanic noticed that your front tires are badly worn. We didn't replace them because we needed your approval first. The car is safe to drive for now, and you can pick it up anytime before six. If you'd like us to put on new tires, call me back by three so we can order them today.","L4423-1.mp3?v=42973e9232"]],"q":"Why did the shop not change the tires?","o":["The owner had not agreed to it yet.","The needed tires were not in stock yet.","The mechanic ran out of time this morning.","The tires were safe enough to keep."],"a":0,"e":"Karen says they did not replace the tires because they needed Daniel's approval first."},{"id":"L4456","k":"k","L":[["M","Good afternoon, visitors. In fifteen minutes, our keepers will feed the sea lions at the outdoor pool next to the Ocean Cafe. It's a great show, and you'll learn how the animals are trained. Seats fill up quickly, so we recommend arriving early. Please note that the first three rows may get wet. Also, the penguin house is closed this afternoon for cleaning, but it will reopen tomorrow morning at nine.","L4456-1.mp3?v=f5df01c243"]],"q":"What does the speaker warn visitors about?","o":["Front seats may be splashed with water.","The show will be canceled if it rains.","The sea lions can be dangerous to touch.","The cafe will close during the show."],"a":0,"e":"The speaker says that people in the first three rows may get wet."},{"id":"L4489","k":"k","L":[["W","This is your Tuesday weather update. It'll be another warm, breezy day with highs near eighty-five. Unfortunately for allergy sufferers, the pollen count is very high, mostly from oak and pine trees, and the wind is spreading it everywhere. If you have allergies, keep your windows closed and try to stay indoors in the early morning, when pollen levels peak. Some relief is on the way: steady rain on Thursday should clear much of it from the air.","L4489-1.mp3?v=a7dd0f6b46"]],"q":"According to the report, when are pollen levels highest?","o":["Soon after the sun comes up","In the middle of the afternoon","During the rain on Thursday","Late in the evening hours"],"a":0,"e":"The reporter says pollen levels peak in the early morning."}]},{"id":"t_mod","sec":"Test","title":"Module test","desc":"Mixed questions, like the real test","items":[{"q":"I ______ on a houseboat in Austria since 1988.","o":["have lived","am","live","am living"],"a":0,"e":"since + a starting point (since 1988): present perfect, have lived."},{"q":"My cat is a real hunter; she ______ anything that moves.","o":["chasing","is chase","chase","chases"],"a":3,"e":"Habit, third person singular, so chases."},{"q":"We ______ the next ECL four weeks from today.","o":["will be have","will have","will had","will be had"],"a":1,"e":"Simple future: will + the simple form of the verb (will have)."},{"q":"I ______ in the Egyptian Navy for six years.","o":["am","am been","have been","has been"],"a":2,"e":"for + a duration up to now takes the present perfect."},{"q":"My teacher ______ to the graduation ceremony tomorrow.","o":["going","goes","is going","is go"],"a":2,"e":"A fixed arrangement -> present progressive with future meaning."},{"q":"My grandkids ______ the Internet right now, so you can't use the phone.","o":["surfing","surf","surfs","are surfing"],"a":3,"e":"right now -> present progressive."},{"q":"Craig and his family ______ in Buenos Aires last year at this time.","o":["were","was","has been","have been"],"a":0,"e":"Plural subject in the past, so were."},{"q":"According to the drill instructor, the trainees ______ the barracks right now.","o":["are cleaning","cleans","is cleaning","was cleaning"],"a":0,"e":"Plural subject with right now."},{"q":"I ______ to the Cherry Tree Festival next year in Japan.","o":["went","am go","am going","have gone"],"a":2,"e":"A settled plan -> be going to."},{"q":"There ______ a lot of sniper attacks here in the last three months.","o":["are","was","is","have been"],"a":3,"e":"in the last three months takes the present perfect, plural."},{"q":"Q: Does your father still live in Lisbon? A: No, he ______ in Norway.","o":["live","living","is live","lives"],"a":3,"e":"Third person singular (he): lives."},{"q":"A: Does your family own a house? B: Neither. My family ______ an apartment.","o":["rent","rents","renting","is rent"],"a":1,"e":"Family is a singular collective, so rents."},{"q":"Q: Does your brother have dimples? A: No, he ______ dimples.","o":["hasn't","hadn't","doesn't have","doesn't has"],"a":2,"e":"Negative of have as a full verb in the present."},{"q":"Surprisingly, the people of that country ______ any gum disease.","o":["doesn't have","don't have","hasn't","isn't having"],"a":1,"e":"People is plural, so don't have."},{"q":"Q: Has Petty Officer Vance removed the device? A: No, he ______ removed it yet.","o":["doesn't have","don't have","hasn't","haven't"],"a":2,"e":"Tag question on the present perfect, singular."},{"q":"Q: How much area has the river flooded? A: The river ______ flooded any area at all.","o":["doesn't have","don't have","hasn't","haven't"],"a":2,"e":"Present perfect negative, singular."},{"q":"Q: How many times did he have a score below 60? A: He ______ any scores below 60.","o":["didn't has","don't have","didn't have","haven't"],"a":2,"e":"The answer repeats the simple past of the question: didn't have."},{"q":"Q: ______ he ever passed the ECL? A: Yes, one time.","o":["Does","Was","Has","Did"],"a":2,"e":"ever + experience -> present perfect."},{"q":"Q: Does he have to take it again? A: Yes, he ______ to take it again.","o":["have","has","doesn't have","hasn't"],"a":1,"e":"Tag question on have to, singular."},{"q":"When I arrived home from school, the postman ______ a small parcel.","o":["was deliver","delivers","delivering","had delivered"],"a":3,"e":"An action earlier than another past action."},{"q":"Everybody ______ going to the dentist.","o":["dislikes","disliking","are dislike","is dislike"],"a":0,"e":"Everybody takes a singular verb."},{"q":"I ______ to the airport tomorrow.","o":["going","went","will go","am go"],"a":2,"e":"Simple future: will + the simple form of the verb (will go)."},{"q":"I ______ a good movie last night.","o":["see","saw","seeing","seen"],"a":1,"e":"\"Last night\" requires *past tense*."},{"q":"I ______ in the military for 6 years.","o":["is","am","are","have been"],"a":3,"e":"for 6 years, up to now: present perfect."},{"q":"By the time you graduate next month, you ______ at least 20 ECL tests.","o":["will have taken","will be take","will have took","are taking"],"a":0,"e":"By the time + a future time: future perfect (will have taken)."},{"q":"He ______ promoted in 2005.","o":["got","get","is got","gotten"],"a":0,"e":"Informal passive with get in the past."},{"q":"The privates ______ lunch right now.","o":["are eating","eats","eating","was eating"],"a":0,"e":"right now with a plural subject."},{"q":"I ______ Brussels next year.","o":["visited","am visiting","did visit","have visit"],"a":1,"e":"A settled plan -> present progressive with future meaning."},{"q":"By this time next year, I ______ all my exams.","o":["will take","will have taken","have taken","take"],"a":1,"e":"By this time next year -> future perfect."},{"q":"While I was driving to work this morning, I ______ about my briefing.","o":["think","was think","will think","was thinking"],"a":3,"e":"Two actions in progress at the same time: past progressive."},{"q":"Before the firemen could extinguish the flames, the house ______.","o":["will already burn down","was already burn down","is already burn down","had already burned down"],"a":3,"e":"An earlier action in the past."},{"q":"First, I went to the movie; then, I ______ some pizza.","o":["eat","will eat","ate","am eating"],"a":2,"e":"A sequence of past actions: simple past."},{"q":"Because it was raining, we ______ the picnic.","o":["cancel","canceled","are cancel","cancels"],"a":1,"e":"Backshift of tense into the past."},{"q":"I ______ the taste of raw tomatoes ever since I was a little boy.","o":["like","am like","liking","have liked"],"a":3,"e":"ever since -> present perfect."},{"q":"I need to borrow some money because I ______ to bring my wallet this morning.","o":["forget","am forget","will forget","forgot"],"a":3,"e":"this morning is a finished period -> simple past."},{"q":"While I was in college, I ______ on most of my tests.","o":["cheat","have cheat","cheated","am cheating"],"a":2,"e":"A finished period in the past: simple past."},{"q":"You may leave now, unless you ______ to hear the same lecture again.","o":["wanted","want","are wanting","will be wanted"],"a":1,"e":"After unless, use the present simple."},{"q":"Just as I was walking into the classroom, the bell ______.","o":["ring","ringing","rang","has rung"],"a":2,"e":"A short action that interrupts another one: simple past (rang)."},{"q":"I will sit in the car and wait while you ______ in the store.","o":["shops","shopped","will be shop","shop"],"a":3,"e":"After while with future meaning, use the present simple."},{"q":"Just as I walked outside, it ______ to rain.","o":["started","starts","starting","is start"],"a":0,"e":"Backshift of tense into the past."},{"q":"Before I mail this letter tomorrow, I ______ it.","o":["am reread","will reread","did reread","rereading"],"a":1,"e":"The main clause is in the future."},{"q":"I was sitting in my car when ______.","o":["the storm start","starts the storm","the storm started","the storm is start"],"a":2,"e":"Subject-verb order + simple past."},{"q":"While you are taking the ECL tomorrow, I ______ your papers.","o":["read","was reading","will be reading","have read"],"a":2,"e":"An action in progress at a future moment -> future progressive."},{"q":"My mother ______ the carpet when I got home yesterday afternoon.","o":["is hoovering","was hoovering","were hoovering","has been hoovering"],"a":1,"e":"An action in progress that was interrupted: past progressive."},{"q":"We ______ the flight tickets yet.","o":["don't book","hasn't booked","have booked","haven't booked"],"a":3,"e":"yet goes with the present perfect negative."},{"q":"I was answering the phone and didn't realize you ______ outside.","o":["wait","were waiting","had waited","are waiting"],"a":1,"e":"An action in progress in the past."},{"q":"Deborah ______ a car before she went to New Zealand.","o":["had have","had had","have had","has had"],"a":1,"e":"Earlier action, so the past perfect of have."},{"q":"Sony offered Sabine a job before she ______ her degree.","o":["finish","had finished","was finishing","finishes"],"a":1,"e":"An earlier action in the past."},{"q":"I had breakfast quite early, then I ______ to the bus stop and caught the bus.","o":["had gone","had went","went","goed"],"a":2,"e":"A sequence of actions: simple past."},{"q":"By the end of this year, I ______ enough money to buy a computer.","o":["will save","save","will have saved","had saved"],"a":2,"e":"By the end of -> future perfect."}]}]};
